{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VMvJmmeicoLQmjfXdBTMDi","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I found the experiment plan and the worst-tier scenario file. Let me now compile the complete findings for you.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully located and read the experiment plan file and the \"worst tier\" scenario definitions. Here are the complete findings:\n\n### Main Experiment Plan File\n**Location:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\nThe experiment plan contains **10 completed experiments** (plan_001 through plan_009, plus plan_011-013) and **1 in-progress experiment** (plan_010):\n\n**Completed Experiments:**\n- **plan_001**: SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO (Status: done, Result: RSA=0.615 >> VLA 0.488 >> DINO 0.388)\n- **plan_002**: DINO baseline RSA (Status: done, Result: RSA=0.388)\n- **plan_003**: Per-layer RSA curve analysis (Status: done, trained peak inverted-U at L12=0.628, untrained monotonic decay)\n- **plan_004**: Output head analysis (Status: done, Projector frozen cos_sim=1.0, LLM weights uniformly distributed)\n- **plan_005**: 6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks verification (Status: done, All 6 methods consistent: trained ≈ untrained >> DINO)\n- **plan_006**: Instruction ablation (Status: done, Δ=0.004 << 0.10 threshold)\n- **plan_007**: 2×2 matrix (training × instruction) (Status: done, All 4 cells ≈ 0.48-0.49)\n- **plan_008**: Random instruction control (Status: done, Instruction content invariant ±0.017)\n- **plan_009**: CKA verification (Status: done, CKA-RSA dissociation found)\n- **plan_011**: Full-layer R² scan (Status: done, R² inverted-U pattern confirmed, peaks at L8/L13)\n- **plan_012**: CLIP-ViT pretraining control (Status: done, CLIP RSA=0.557 < DINO)\n- **plan_013**: Branch-split RSA (Status: done, DINOv2≈SigLIP, both contribute equally)\n\n**In Progress:**\n- **plan_010**: LIBERO-Spatial benchmark extension (Status: preparing, Data download + disk cleanup in progress)\n\n### \"Worst Tier\" Scenario File\n**Location:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260522T021705/worst/imagined_experiments.yaml`\n\nThis file contains a comprehensive worst-case scenario analysis with the following key sections:\n\n1. **Narrative Guidance**: Describes the worst-case reviewer attacks focusing on:\n   - Cross-architecture evidence being insufficient or trivial\n   - R² exit collapse being a generic decoder-only architecture effect rather than VLA-specific\n   - OpenVLA Spatial showing weak results (RUNNING experiment)\n   - Matrix having missing cells (NORA Object/Long absent)\n   - Only 1 Tier-2 data point for the three-tier gradient claim\n   - Complete lack of behavioral validation\n\n2. **Imagined Experiments** (20 detailed scenarios including):\n   - Critical experiments with worst-case interpretations\n   - Expected reviewer critiques and attack surfaces\n   - Missing control experiments (e.g., NLP fine-tuned LLM baseline)\n   - Architectural coverage limitations\n\n3. **Cross-Architecture R² Exit Collapse Matrix**:\n   - 10/12 cells filled (NORA Object/Long missing)\n   - Only 6/10 cells show clear collapse (delta > 0.10)\n   - 4/10 cells show weak or absent collapse\n   - Delta range: 0.004–0.691 (172x range, not \"consistent\")\n   - Peak layer std dev: 6.2 (high architectural variability)\n\n4. **Key Worst-Tier Findings**:\n   - **D090 Analysis**: L1 routing (0→9→24 heads) is base-model-dependent, not training-induced\n   - **Only 2 training-induced effects remain**: R² exit collapse (questionable VLA-specificity) and CF sensitivity (unfair baseline comparison)\n   - **Contribution after D090**: Too thin for CoRL acceptance\n   - **Expected reviewer verdict**: 2 rejects + 1 weak accept (mean score 3.67, likely reject)\n\n5. **Proposed Framework Reframe**: The document suggests repositioning the paper from \"VLA-specific architecture analysis\" to \"A Systematic Framework for Analyzing Instruction Processing in VLAs\" to strengthen the contribution narrative.\n\nThe worst-tier scenario is highly detailed and strategic, serving as a guide for anticipating reviewer criticisms and planning countermeasures for paper submission to CoRL."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4327d556-6a05-42fb-ae30-82d4a0777322","uuid":"90ef23e1-2ff3-4f48-9c18-5d7c4047efd3","timestamp":"2026-05-27T02:51:49.915Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the directory /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15, find and read the experiment_plan file (likely YAML or markdown) that contains all planned experiments with their IDs, claims, descriptions, etc. Also look for any file that defines the \"worst\" tier predictions or scenario definitions. Search broadly - check for files like experiment_plan.yaml, experiment_plan.md, plans/, etc. Report the full content of the experiment plan.","agentId":"ab65d27d3f59ed027","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I found the experiment plan and the worst-tier scenario file. Let me now compile the complete findings for you.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully located and read the experiment plan file and the \"worst tier\" scenario definitions. Here are the complete findings:\n\n### Main Experiment Plan File\n**Location:** `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/experiment_plan.yaml`\n\nThe experiment plan contains **10 completed experiments** (plan_001 through plan_009, plus plan_011-013) and **1 in-progress experiment** (plan_010):\n\n**Completed Experiments:**\n- **plan_001**: SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO (Status: done, Result: RSA=0.615 >> VLA 0.488 >> DINO 0.388)\n- **plan_002**: DINO baseline RSA (Status: done, Result: RSA=0.388)\n- **plan_003**: Per-layer RSA curve analysis (Status: done, trained peak inverted-U at L12=0.628, untrained monotonic decay)\n- **pla