{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012iCJPUbW55yzctfHiUfetM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the complete picture. Let me generate the full worst-tier predictions based on the updated D096/D099/D100/D102 findings and the actual registry data.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Reviewers 认为 exit collapse 是 trivially expected（VLM→VLA 当然改变表征），CF 无 behavioral grounding 缺乏 functional significance，\n  论文被视为 descriptive analysis without actionable insight。D100 NLP control（Llama-2-chat ΔR²=0.000）虽然排除了 generic fine-tuning\n  confound，但 worst-tier reviewer 将此重新解读为：\"好，exit collapse 不是 generic fine-tuning 的——但它仍然是 trivially expected\n  的 VLM→VLA transition effect。当你把 language model 改造成 action model，出口层表征当然会重组——这不需要你的 framework 来'发现'。\"\n  D102 的 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 二元分离被反过来论证：\"你自己证明了 exit collapse 是 one-time transition artifact，不是 ongoing\n  routing mechanism。它在 VLA→VLA finetuning 时消失（0/4），说明它不是 functional routing signature 而是 initial adaptation shock。\n  这反而削弱了 exit collapse 作为 'diagnostic tool' 的价值——它只能告诉你 '这个模型曾经从 VLM 变成 VLA'，这在实践中谁不知道？\"\n  Reframe 方向：从 \"discovering routing mechanisms\" 转为 \"diagnostic methodology for VLA development\"。核心 pitch 变为：\n  本文提供第一个系统化的 VLA representational profiling toolkit，跨 3 架构验证。但 worst-tier 下即使此 reframe 也被质疑：\n  \"一个 diagnostic framework 如果主要发现是 trivially expected（exit collapse）和 functionally unvalidated（CF sensitivity），\n  那 framework 的 utility 在哪里？你需要 demonstrate 这个 framework 能发现 non-obvious actionable insights。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA 对比 Full VLA 和 DINO，证明 action-relevant 结构源自 frozen vision encoder\"\n    expected_results:\n      siglip_projector_rsa: 0.615\n      trained_with_inst_rsa: 0.488\n      untrained_with_inst_rsa: 0.485\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      llm_degradation_delta: 0.127\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据已完成不变。在 worst 档下，此实验仅覆盖 OpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP encoder。Reviewer 攻击路线：\n      \"SigLIP+Projector RSA=0.615 是 OpenVLA-specific frozen encoder 的观察。TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision encoder，\n      NORA 用 InternViT——你们没测这些 encoder 的 RSA。单架构 encoder analysis 无法 claim architecture-independent。\"\n      LLM degradation（0.615→0.488）本身被视为 \"trivially expected—— LLM 的 intermediate processing 当然会\n      改变 representation geometry，这不是 finding 而是 definition。\" 在 diagnostic framework reframe 下，\n      此实验降为 \"framework 在 OpenVLA 上的 case study\"——不再是 core contribution。更致命的是，Reviewer 会用\n      这个实验反过来攻击论文 motivation：\"如果 frozen encoder 已经提供了最好的 action-relevant structure（RSA=0.615），\n      而 LLM processing 只是 degrade 它（到 0.488），那为什么要研究 LLM 内部的 instruction routing？问题不在 routing\n      而在 LLM 设计本身——你应该研究如何让 LLM 不 degrade encoder output。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SigLIP RSA Scope Limitation (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"RSA\", \"Architecture Coverage\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SigLIP+Proj\", \"0.615\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Cannot generalize to other VLA encoders\"]\n          - [\"VLA trained\", \"0.488\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Llama-2-specific LLM degradation\"]\n          - [\"VLA untrained\", \"0.485\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Random-init Llama-2 specific\"]\n          - [\"DINO\", \"0.388\", \"Standalone\", \"Reference baseline, unaffected\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart 标注 'OpenVLA only' 在每个 bar 上方，突显 single-arch limitation\"\n    analysis: |\n      Framework reframe 下此实验从 C1 core evidence 降为 Section 4.1 case study。价值在于 demonstrate\n      framework 的 encoder-LLM decomposition 能力，而非 claim 本身。Reviewer 不会因此给分但也不会因此扣分——\n      neutral contribution in worst tier。但 LLM degradation finding 可能被用来攻击论文 motivation 本身。\n\n  - name: \"DINO baseline RSA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"Standalone vision model 参照基线\"\n    expected_results:\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      dino_action_R2: 0.687\n      dino_subtask_auc: 0.972\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。Worst 档下 DINO 的角色被 weaponize：R²=0.687 对比 VLA 训练后的 exit R² drop。Reviewer：\n      \"DINO（self-supervised, 无 language, 无 action training）的 action probe R²=0.687 已经很高，\n      说明 action prediction 主要是 visual task。你们声称的 VLA 训练重组 instruction routing，但如果一个\n      纯视觉模型无需任何 instruction 就能达到 R²=0.687，instruction routing 的 practical value 是什么？\n      这反而证明了 Grant et al. 2026 的 visual dominance finding——instructions 在 VLA 中可能根本不重要。\"\n      DINO subtask AUC=0.972 进一步强化这个论点——task progress 几乎完全可从 visual features 预测，\n      无需 instruction information。这直接攻击论文研究 instruction routing 的 premise。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"DINO R²=0.687 标注在所有 cross-arch R² exit collapse 图上作为 'no-language baseline'\"\n    analysis: |\n      Worst tier 下 DINO baseline 被用来论证整篇论文的 premise 可疑：如果 vision alone 足够好，\n      instruction routing research 的 practical relevance 被严重削弱。Framework reframe 可以\n      acknowledge 但无法完全化解这个攻击。\n\n  - name: \"Per-layer RSA degradation curve\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹\"\n    expected_results:\n      proj_rsa: 0.615\n      trained_peak_rsa: 0.488\n      trained_peak_layer: 9\n      untrained_peak_rsa: 0.485\n      untrained_peak_layer: 12\n      proj_to_l1_drop: 0.13\n      inverted_u_trained: true\n      inverted_u_untrained: true\n      rise_phase_delta: 0.016\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。Worst 档下 inverted-U 只在 OpenVLA (Llama-2) 上验证过，TracVLA/NORA 的 RSA per-layer\n      curve 从未做过。CKA 在 plan_009 中反转了 RSA ordering（untrained > trained），使 RSA metric 的\n      authority 受损。Rise phase Δρ=0.016 极小（CI 可能 includes 0），reviewer 会指出：\n      \"你声称 training shifts RSA peak from L0 to L12，但 rise phase 只有 0.016 ρ——这在 noise level 内。\n      如果 CKA 不支持 inverted-U，你不能 claim 这是 robust pattern——这是 metric-specific artifact。\"\n      在 CoRL（robotics venue），per-layer RSA curve 被视为 \"interesting visualization but not\n      contribution\"——reviewer 期望功能性验证而非几何观察。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSA Inverted-U Architecture Coverage\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"RSA Per-Layer Done?\", \"Pattern\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B)\", \"Yes\", \"Inverted-U\", \"Only confirmed case, CKA reversal undermines\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3-mini)\", \"No\", \"Unknown\", \"Cannot claim generalization\"]\n          - [\"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)\", \"No\", \"Unknown\", \"Cannot claim generalization\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer RSA curve 只有 OpenVLA 一条线，旁注 'CKA reversal: untrained > trained'\"\n    analysis: |\n      Inverted-U 成为 C3 observation 的核心证据但被 metric-dependence 严重削弱。\n      Framework reframe 下可保留为 \"framework reveals metric-dependent patterns\"\n      但这同时 undermine 了 framework 发现的 authority——如果换个 metric 结论就变，framework 的可靠性如何？\n\n  - name: \"Output head analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"SigLIP+projector frozen 确认, LLM 权重变化不传导到表征\"\n    expected_results:\n      vision_projector_cos_sim: 1.0\n      llm_rel_change_mean: 1.316\n      llm_rel_change_range: [1.22, 1.37]\n      head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n      shallow_adaptation_gate: \"FAIL\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。Worst 档下此实验被视为 trivial verification：\"OpenVLA 代码 freeze 了 vision encoder，\n      你只是验证了代码做了它该做的事。cos_sim=1.0 不是 finding，是 implementation check。\"\n      LLM 权重均匀分布（1.22-1.37）也不 surprising——\"random init vs pretrained 的差异当然大且均匀，\n      这是 comparing random weights to structured weights，不是 analyzing fine-tuning effects。\n      你的 caveat 自己也说了：comparison is pretrained Llama + fine-tune vs random init，\n      所以 differences dominated by pretrained vs random，not by VLA training.\"\n      在 8-page limit 下，worst tier 建议此实验压缩为半段或移到 appendix。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      贡献接近零。Framework reframe 下可作为 \"component attribution capability\" 的 one-sentence\n      mention。不值得独立分析。\n\n  - name: \"6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks 系统验证\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained 表征结构\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_untrained_rsa_delta: 0.003\n      trained_untrained_r2_delta: 0.015\n      cka_ordering_reversal: true\n      all_methods_show_vla_gt_dino: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Orphaned 但子实验（RSA, R², CKA, action probe, delta probe, classification）均已完成。\n      Worst 档下 trained ≈ untrained 被视为 \"trivially expected under frozen encoder\"。\n      Reviewer：\"frozen SigLIP+projector 输出相同 L0 features，LLM fine-tuning 只改变 weights\n      而非 input distribution——所以 intermediate layer representations naturally similar。\n      你用 6 种方法验证一个 structurally guaranteed result，这不是 thoroughness 而是 over-verification。\"\n      CKA ordering reversal 进一步削弱 multi-method consistency narrative——6 methods 中 CKA\n      反转了 RSA，说明 \"consistency\" 是 cherry-picked（只 consistent 在某些 metrics 下）。\n      Worst reviewer 总结：\"这些实验证明了 VLA > DINO 但 trained ≈ untrained——\n      前者 expected（LLM 有 4096d features vs DINO 1024d），后者 也 expected（same encoder）。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"6 Methods Under Worst-Tier Reinterpretation\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Trained-Untrained Δ\", \"Worst Reviewer Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA (geometric)\", \"0.003\", \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"]\n          - [\"R² action probe\", \"+0.015\", \"Marginal: within noise\"]\n          - [\"CKA (global)\", \"-0.006\", \"REVERSAL: undermines RSA narrative\"]\n          - [\"Action probe (MLP)\", \"+0.045\", \"Small routing effect, not surprising\"]\n          - [\"Delta probe\", \"+0.011\", \"Same encoder → similar structure\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"+0.001\", \"Trivially easy for both conditions\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"6-method consistency radar chart 标注 'CKA reversal' 打破 perfect consistency 叙事\"\n    analysis: |\n      6 methods consistency 从 \"strong evidence for trained ≈ untrained\" 降为\n      \"thorough but unsurprising verification of a structurally predicted outcome\"。\n      CKA reversal 使 \"all methods consistent\" claim 不成立。Framework reframe 下\n      唯一残余价值：demonstrate framework 的 multi-method coverage capability。\n\n  - name: \"Instruction ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\"\n    expected_results:\n      delta_with_vs_no_inst: 0.004\n      gate_judgment: \"FAIL — instruction 无影响 on RSA\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。Worst 档下被视为 tautological sanity check：image token RSA 在 causal mask 下\n      不受 instruction tokens 影响是 structural guarantee，不是 empirical finding。\n      Reviewer：\"你在 C1 里承认 causal mask 使 image tokens 看不到 instructions，\n      然后在 plan_006 里'发现' image RSA 不受 instructions 影响——这是验证了你自己的前提假设。\n      Δ=0.004 是 noise，不是 small effect——effect 在结构上不可能存在。\n      这 0.5 页可以省掉或用一句话带过。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Worst tier 下从 C3 evidence 降为 \"confirms structural prediction, not finding\"。\n      Framework reframe 下可作为 \"sanity check\" 一句带过，不占独立段落。\n\n  - name: \"2×2 matrix (training × instruction)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"四条件全收敛验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_with_inst: 0.488\n      trained_no_inst: 0.489\n      untrained_with_inst: 0.485\n      untrained_no_inst: 0.480\n      bootstrap_ci_includes_0: true\n      training_effect: 0.003\n      instruction_effect: 0.004\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。Worst 档下 2×2 null result 被视为 \"expected outcome of frozen encoder + causal mask\"。\n      Reviewer：\"你的 2×2 factorial design 是好的 experimental methodology，但它发现了 predicted null——\n      both factors (training, instruction) have no effect on image token RSA 因为 (1) encoder frozen,\n      (2) causal mask blocks instruction→image. 好的 experimental design + expected null result\n      = methodology paper contribution, not empirical contribution。如果这是 methodology paper\n      那 ok，但你 pitch 的是 empirical findings about VLA routing。\"\n      四条件收敛到 0.48-0.49 band 进一步证实 RSA 对 image tokens 是 ceiling+floor bounded by encoder quality。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 Matrix as Expected Null (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"RSA\", \"Reviewer Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained + Inst\", \"0.488\", \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"]\n          - [\"Trained - Inst\", \"0.489\", \"Expected: causal mask blocks\"]\n          - [\"Untrained + Inst\", \"0.485\", \"Expected: same encoder\"]\n          - [\"Untrained - Inst\", \"0.480\", \"Expected: both factors null\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 heatmap 标注 'Predicted null under frozen encoder hypothesis'\"\n    analysis: |\n      Framework reframe 下 2×2 matrix 的价值从 \"finding\" 转为 \"exemplar of factorial\n      design capability\"——可复用性贡献，但在 CoRL 不计高分。\n\n  - name: \"Random instruction control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"随机/无意义 instruction 替代验证 RSA 不受 instruction content 影响\"\n    expected_results:\n      normal_rsa: 0.489\n      random_rsa: 0.484\n      shuffled_rsa: 0.483\n      empty_rsa: 0.472\n      max_absolute_delta: 0.017\n      instruction_invariant: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。与 plan_006/007 同一逻辑链——causal mask 使 image token RSA 对 instruction content\n      天然不变。Worst reviewer：\"你用了三个 experiments（006/007/008）验证同一个 structurally guaranteed\n      null result。Normal/random/shuffled/empty 全在 ±0.02 内不是 finding，是 noise around a\n      guaranteed null。这占了论文篇幅但不增加 contribution。在 8 页限制下，三个实验应压缩为 1 段 sanity check。\"\n      更刻薄的 reviewer：\"spending 3 experiments on 'image tokens don't see instruction tokens'\n      suggests the authors don't fully understand their own architecture's causal mask structure.\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      006/007/008 三合一压缩为半段。Framework reframe 下仅作为 \"invariance verification\"\n      methodology demo。在 worst tier 下浪费篇幅的风险 > 贡献。\n\n  - name: \"CKA verification\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"CKA 指标验证 RSA 发现的 metric robustness\"\n    expected_results:\n      linear_cka_ordering: \"untrained > trained > projector > DINO\"\n      rsa_ordering: \"projector > trained > untrained > DINO\"\n      ordering_reversal: true\n      last_preaction_cka: 0.127\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。CKA-RSA dissociation 在 worst 档下变得 doubly 致命。\n      第一层攻击（保持不变）：\"如果 CKA 说 untrained > trained 而 RSA 说 trained > untrained，\n      那哪个 metric 才反映 'action-relevant information'？你选了 RSA 来讲 story，但另一个\n      equally principled metric 给出相反结论。这不是 metric dissociation finding——\n      这是 your conclusions are metric-dependent 的 admission。\"\n      第二层攻击（D095 升级后更致命）：\"你们现在 claim R² exit collapse 是跨架构一致的\n      VLM→VLA signature。但 R² 本身是 functional metric（probe-based），RSA 是 geometric metric，\n      CKA 是 kernel-based metric。如果不同 metrics 给不同结论，你凭什么用 R² 的 exit collapse\n      而不是 CKA 的 no-collapse 来 claim 'architecture-independent signature'？\n      你的 framework 应该 reconcile 这些 metrics 而不是 pick 对你有利的那个。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Metric Ordering Reversal (Worst-Tier Authority Crisis)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Ordering\", \"Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA (geometric)\", \"SigLIP > T > U > DINO\", \"Training degrades geometry\"]\n          - [\"CKA (global)\", \"U > T > SigLIP > DINO\", \"Training preserves/improves structure\"]\n          - [\"R² (functional)\", \"T_lastpre > DINO ≈ Proj > T_img > U\", \"Training enables routing\"]\n          - [\"Reviewer question\", \"—\", \"Framework credibility if metrics disagree?\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Triple ordering diagram 标注 contradiction arrows between RSA and CKA\"\n    analysis: |\n      CKA dissociation 在 worst tier 下是 double-edged：可以包装为 \"why we need multi-metric\n      framework\" 但同时 undermines 所有 single-metric conclusions。Exit collapse 只在 R²\n      下明显——如果 CKA 下不 collapse，reviewer 要求 \"architecture-independent\" 必须\n      \"metric-independent\"，否则 claim 降级。\n\n  - name: \"LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark 扩展\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"第三个 benchmark（LIBERO-Spatial）交叉验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.696\n      trained_image_mean_peak_layer: 13\n      trained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.675\n      trained_last_preaction_peak_layer: 21\n      untrained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.673\n      untrained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.635\n      trained_vs_untrained_delta_imgmean: 0.023\n      trained_vs_untrained_delta_lastpre: 0.040\n      bootstrap_p: 0.001\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据已完成。Worst 档下此实验是 within-architecture cross-benchmark（仍是 OpenVLA），\n      不解决 RC4 的 cross-architecture concern。Reviewer：\"从 LIBERO-Goal 换到 LIBERO-Spatial\n      只是换了 task suite 不是换了 VLA 架构——这不回答 'does it generalize across architectures'。\"\n      Spatial 的 trained-untrained delta（best-vs-best）=0.023（imgmean）/ 0.040（lastpre）\n      小于 Goal 的 0.015/0.069。退一步看，R² exit collapse 在 D102 更新后被重新定义为\n      VLM→VLA transition effect——但 LIBERO-Spatial 和 Goal 都用同一个 OpenVLA checkpoint（已是 VLA），\n      所以 trained vs untrained（OXE vs LIBERO-finetuned）的 delta 本就该小（VLA→VLA transition）。\n      这与 D102 结论一致但在 worst tier 下被解读为 \"further fine-tuning doesn't change much\n      = fine-tuning doesn't matter much = your study of fine-tuning effects is studying something trivial。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Benchmark Comparison (OpenVLA Only)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Delta (imgmean best-vs-best)\", \"Delta (lastpre best-vs-best)\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LIBERO-Goal\", \"0.015\", \"0.069\", \"Moderate; only architecture tested\"]\n          - [\"LIBERO-Spatial\", \"0.023\", \"0.040\", \"Small; confirms VLA→VLA transition minimal\"]\n          - [\"Implication\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Within-arch replication, not cross-arch validation\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side R² curves for Goal vs Spatial 标注 both are OpenVLA\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cross-benchmark replication 有价值但不解决 cross-architecture gap。D102 framing 下\n      small delta 是 expected（VLA→VLA），但 reviewer 会用此攻击：\"如果进一步 finetuning\n      不 substantially change representations，studying finetuning effects 的意义何在？\"\n\n  - name: \"Full-layer R² scan\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations = 132 probes 的 R² 全层扫描\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 8, R2: 0.655}\n      trained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 13, R2: 0.678}\n      untrained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 0, R2: 0.640}\n      untrained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 32, R2: 0.609}\n      trained_exit_R2_lastpre: 0.422\n      untrained_exit_R2_lastpre: 0.545\n      exit_collapse_delta_lastpre: 0.256\n      best_vs_best_lastpre_delta: 0.069\n      best_vs_best_lastpre_p: 0.0001\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变（OpenVLA 单架构）。这是 R² exit collapse 的源头实验。D100 NLP control 已排除\n      generic fine-tuning confound（Llama-2-chat ΔR²=0.000），D102 将其定义为 VLM→VLA transition effect。\n      但 worst-tier reviewer 反转 D100/D102：\n      \"D100 证明 NLP finetuning 不产生 exit collapse——好。但这只说明 exit collapse 需要 action training，\n      不说明它有 functional significance。VLM→VLA transition 当然改变 exit layer——action head 需要从\n      exit layer decode 7-DOF actions，这不是 routing 'discovery' 而是 'the model learned to produce actions\n      and the last layer reflects that'。你的 R² probe 测量的是 Ridge regression 从 hidden states 预测 actions\n      的能力——exit layer R² 下降只是说明 action-relevant information 被 'consumed' by action decoding，\n      不是被 'discarded' by routing mechanism。这是 trivially expected under any encoder-decoder framework。\"\n      Worst reviewer 要求 behavioral evidence：如果 exit collapse 是 functional routing，\n      ablating exit-layer representations 应该 disproportionately affect task performance——但这从未被测试。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"R² Exit Collapse with D100/D102 Context (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Peak R²\", \"Exit R²\", \"Δ\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"VLA trained\", \"0.678 (L13)\", \"0.422 (L32)\", \"0.256\", \"Action head 'consumes' info — trivially expected\"]\n          - [\"OXE untrained\", \"0.609 (L32)\", \"0.609 (L32)\", \"0.000\", \"No exit collapse — consistent with VLA→VLA null\"]\n          - [\"Llama-2-chat (D100)\", \"0.156 (all)\", \"0.156 (all)\", \"0.000\", \"NLP: flat noise floor, no action info anywhere\"]\n          - [\"Random init\", \"0.640 (L0)\", \"~0 (L10-L13)\", \"pathological\", \"Not valid control — random weights meaningless\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer R² curves with NLP control flat line at 0.155, annotated 'trivially expected action consumption'\"\n    analysis: |\n      D100 NLP control 排除了 generic fine-tuning confound，这是论文的防御性胜利。但 worst reviewer\n      的 next-level 攻击——exit collapse 是 \"action consumption\" 而非 \"routing mechanism\"——\n      仍然 stands without behavioral validation。Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge 这个区分\n      并 position exit collapse 为 \"diagnostic indicator of action training stage\" 而非 \"mechanistic finding\"。\n\n  - name: \"CLIP-ViT pretraining control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP 区分 VL pretraining vs encoder quality\"\n    expected_results:\n      clip_rsa: 0.557\n      clip_R2: 0.587\n      dino_cls_rsa: 0.692\n      dino_cls_R2: 0.634\n      projector_R2: 0.630\n      vl_pretraining_not_superior: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据已完成：CLIP < DINO in both RSA and R²。VL pretraining 不优于 self-supervised。\n      Worst 档延伸攻击：\"CLIP < DINO 说明 language-supervised pretraining 不帮助 action representation。\n      那为什么 VLA 要用 language-supervised encoder（SigLIP）而非 self-supervised（DINO）？更关键的是：\n      如果最好的 action-relevant encoder 不需要 language，你们花整篇论文研究 instruction routing\n      的 practical relevance 在哪里？Instructions 在 VLA 中可能是 overhead 而非 feature。\n      你们应该研究为什么 VLA 不用 DINO 作为 encoder，而非研究 instruction 如何 route through LLM。\"\n      这直接挑战论文 premise 而非 findings——worst tier 下论文可能被判 \"interesting but\n      fundamentally misdirected\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Encoder Quality vs Language Supervision\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder\", \"RSA\", \"R²\", \"Has Language?\", \"Worst Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"DINO cls\", \"0.692\", \"0.634\", \"No\", \"Best in both — language supervision unnecessary\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP+Proj\", \"0.615\", \"0.630\", \"Yes\", \"VL pretraining inferior to DINO\"]\n          - [\"CLIP ViT-L\", \"0.557\", \"0.587\", \"Yes\", \"Worst VL encoder\"]\n          - [\"Implication\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Language supervision may hurt encoder quality\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"DINO vs VL encoders scatter plot — DINO dominates upper-right corner\"\n    analysis: |\n      CLIP control 结果在 worst tier 下不仅否定 VL pretraining superiority，更挑战整篇论文的\n      motivation。Framework reframe 可以 spin 为 \"framework reveals that language supervision\n      and action quality are decoupled\" 但这是 defensive 而非 proactive contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Branch-split RSA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"DinoSigLIP fused backbone 中 DINOv2 vs SigLIP branch 分离\"\n    expected_results:\n      dinov2_branch_rsa: 0.619\n      siglip_branch_rsa: 0.621\n      fused_rsa: 0.634\n      post_projector_rsa: 0.615\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP in fused backbone（Δ<0.002）。Worst 档下此实验只适用于\n      OpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP 架构。TracVLA 和 NORA 用完全不同的 vision encoders，\n      branch-split 不可迁移。Reviewer：\"这是 architecture-specific implementation detail，\n      不是 generalizable finding。在 8-page 限制下应移到 appendix。\"\n      在 diagnostic framework reframe 下可保留为 \"framework 能做 sub-encoder analysis\" demo，\n      但 0.5 段就够了。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Architecture-specific detail，appendix material。Framework demo 价值存在但不值得 main text 篇幅。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture R² Exit Collapse Matrix (D096/D099/D102)\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_r2_matrix\"\n    description: \"3 架构 × 4 suite 的 R² exit collapse — D102 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 二元分离\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_cells: 10\n      vlm_to_vla_cells: 6\n      vlm_to_vla_all_substantial: true\n      vlm_to_vla_delta_range: [0.156, 0.455]\n      vla_to_vla_cells: 4\n      vla_to_vla_none_substantial: true\n      vla_to_vla_delta_range: [0.033, 0.086]\n      nlp_control_delta: 0.000\n      binary_separation: \"VLM→VLA 6/6 vs VLA→VLA 0/4\"\n      tracvla_goal_delta: 0.228\n      tracvla_spatial_delta: 0.138\n      tracvla_object_delta: 0.294\n      tracvla_long_delta: 0.198\n      nora_goal_delta: 0.691\n      nora_spatial_delta: 0.302\n      openvla_goal_delta: 0.086\n      openvla_spatial_delta: 0.037\n      openvla_object_delta: 0.037\n      openvla_long_delta: 0.033\n    result_rationale: |\n      D102 更新后数据清晰：VLM→VLA transition 6/6 一致（Δ=0.156-0.455），VLA→VLA 0/4 超过 Δ>0.10\n      阈值（Δ=0.033-0.086）。v3 MCCV 修正了 train-test leakage。D100 NLP control ΔR²=0.000\n      排除了 generic fine-tuning confound。\n      \n      但 worst-tier reviewer 用 D102 的 clean binary 反过来攻击：\n      \"你们自己证明了 exit collapse 是 one-time VLM→VLA transition artifact。这很好，但：\n      (1) 这不是 mechanism discovery——当你把 language model 变成 action model，出口层表征\n      当然会重组。任何 domain adaptation（NLP→vision, text→audio）都可能产生类似 transition effects。\n      你排除了 NLP finetuning，但没排除其他 domain adaptation scenarios（e.g., LLM→code generation）。\n      (2) 作为 diagnostic tool 的价值有限：exit collapse 只告诉你 'this model was once a VLM\n      that got converted to VLA'——但在实践中你已经知道这一点（你知道模型的 training pipeline）。\n      什么时候 practitioner 需要一个 tool 来判断 '我的模型是不是 VLA'？\n      (3) VLA→VLA finetuning 无 exit collapse（0/4）说明它不是 ongoing routing optimization 的\n      indicator——它只是 initial adaptation 的 one-time marker。一个只出现一次的 diagnostic \n      不能用于 iterative VLA development。\n      (4) Magnitude 仍然高度 variable（0.156-0.691, 4.4x range even within VLM→VLA cells），\n      NORA 的 0.691 是 outlier（3x median）。Architecture-independent 的 direction 但\n      architecture-dependent 的 magnitude——这降低了作为 quantitative diagnostic 的 precision。\"\n\n      D100 NLP control 是 good defense 但不足以救 worst tier——因为 reviewer 的攻击不是\n      \"exit collapse is generic fine-tuning\" 而是 \"exit collapse is trivially expected VLM→VLA transition\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"R² Exit Collapse: D102 Binary Separation (Worst-Tier Reinterpretation)\"\n        columns: [\"Transition Type\", \"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Δ (peak-exit)\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"TracVLA (Phi-3→VLA)\", \"Goal\", \"0.228\", \"Expected: domain adaptation reorganization\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"TracVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.138\", \"Expected: same mechanism\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"TracVLA\", \"Object\", \"0.294\", \"Expected: same mechanism\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"TracVLA\", \"Long\", \"0.198\", \"Expected: same mechanism\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"NORA (Qwen2.5→VLA)\", \"Goal\", \"0.691\", \"Outlier: 3x median, architecture-specific\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"NORA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.302\", \"Expected: consistent with NORA pattern\"]\n          - [\"VLA→VLA\", \"OpenVLA (OXE→LIBERO)\", \"Goal\", \"0.086\", \"Below threshold: no new collapse\"]\n          - [\"VLA→VLA\", \"OpenVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.037\", \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"]\n          - [\"VLA→VLA\", \"OpenVLA\", \"Object\", \"0.037\", \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"]\n          - [\"VLA→VLA\", \"OpenVLA\", \"Long\", \"0.033\", \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"]\n      - title: \"Exit Collapse Diagnostic Value Assessment\"\n        columns: [\"Question\", \"Answer\", \"Practical Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Does model show VLM→VLA transition?\", \"Yes, 6/6 cells\", \"Low: practitioner already knows training history\"]\n          - [\"Can it track ongoing optimization?\", \"No, 0/4 VLA→VLA cells\", \"Zero: one-time marker only\"]\n          - [\"Is magnitude calibrated?\", \"No, 4.4x range within VLM→VLA\", \"Low: cannot compare across architectures\"]\n          - [\"Does NLP control exclude confound?\", \"Yes, D100 ΔR²=0.000\", \"Defensive win but doesn't add value\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap split into VLM→VLA (warm) vs VLA→VLA (cold) blocks — clean separation but 'trivially expected' annotation\"\n      - \"NORA Goal outlier at 0.691 circled with '3x median' annotation\"\n    analysis: |\n      D102 binary separation 是 scientifically clean 但 worst-tier reviewer 把 clean result\n      重新定义为 trivial result。NLP control 是 necessary defense 但不 sufficient to elevate\n      contribution。Framework reframe：exit collapse 降为 \"one-time transition marker detected\n      by framework\" 而非 \"architecture-independent routing signature\"。价值在 framework 能\n      systematically detect transition effects 而非 the specific effect detected。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture L1 Attention (D090 Base-Model vs Training)\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_l1_attention\"\n    description: \"3 架构 L1 instruction-dominant heads — D090 证明 base-model-dependent\"\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_trained: 23\n      openvla_oxe_untrained: 26\n      tracvla_trained: [27, 30]\n      tracvla_untrained_vlm: 32\n      nora_trained: [12, 13]\n      nora_untrained_vlm: [13, 14]\n      training_effect_on_l1: \"none or negative\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      D090 发现 L1 head count 是 base-model-dependent。Worst tier 核心攻击：\n      \"L1 routing gradient（0→9→24 heads）是论文最 visually striking 的结果，但你们自己证明了\n      它不是训练学到的。TracVLA untrained（纯 VLM）已 32/32，训练反而减少到 27-30（repurposing）。\n      NORA untrained 已 13-14/16，训练无变化。OpenVLA 的 0→24 gradient 只是 random init vs\n      pretrained 的差异——任何 pretrained LLM 都有 instruction attention heads，不需要 VLA training。\n      \n      这意味着论文最核心的 visual result（Figure X 的 attention head gradient）不能 claim\n      是 VLA training 的贡献。读者看到这个图会以为训练创造了 routing——但实际上 routing 来自\n      language pretraining。这是 misleading framing，即使你在正文中有 caveat。\"\n      \n      D090 后 remaining training-induced effects 只剩 exit collapse 和 CF sensitivity。\n      Reviewer 总结：\"After D090, VLA training's unique contribution is one transition artifact\n      (exit collapse) and one baseline-confounded sensitivity measure (CF). This is too thin\n      for a full paper at a top robotics venue.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"L1 Heads: Training Contributes Nothing (D090 Worst Reading)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Base Model\", \"Trained\", \"Untrained\", \"Training Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Llama-2-7B\", \"24/32\", \"0/32 (random init)\", \"Artifact: random has no LM\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"OXE-pretrained\", \"24/32\", \"25/32 (OXE)\", \"-1: OXE already saturated\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Phi-3-mini\", \"27-30/32\", \"32/32 (VLM base)\", \"-2 to -5: training REDUCES\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Qwen2.5-VL-3B\", \"12-13/16\", \"13-14/16\", \"-1: no training effect\"]\n      - title: \"Contribution Audit After D090\"\n        columns: [\"Originally Claimed\", \"Post-D090 Status\", \"Remaining Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"L1 routing gradient (0→9→24)\", \"REMOVED: base-model artifact\", \"Zero\"]\n          - [\"Bookend attention pattern\", \"WEAKENED: entry from base model\", \"Exit engagement only\"]\n          - [\"R² exit collapse\", \"Retained: training-induced\", \"Thin — one-time transition\"]\n          - [\"CF sensitivity\", \"Retained: training-induced\", \"Thin — unfair baselines\"]\n          - [\"Experimental framework\", \"Intact\", \"Main surviving contribution\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Before/After D090 contribution diagram — L1 routing crossed out, remaining pillars marked 'questionable'\"\n    analysis: |\n      D090 是论文最大的 self-inflicted wound。Framework reframe 试图把 D090 从 weakness 转为\n      \"framework's key capability: distinguishing training-induced from pre-existing\"——\n      但 reviewer 可能看穿这个 rhetorical move。核心问题：能区分 training vs pretraining\n      effects 是 methodology 贡献，但 CoRL 评审 findings 而非 methods。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture Counterfactual Sensitivity\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_cf\"\n    description: \"3 架构 CF sensitivity — trained vs untrained 对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_goal_trained_d: 1.182\n      openvla_goal_untrained_d: 1.048\n      openvla_spatial_trained_d: 1.173\n      openvla_spatial_untrained_d: 0.936\n      tracvla_goal_trained_d: 1.524\n      tracvla_goal_untrained_cos: 0.153\n      nora_goal_trained_cos: 1.0\n      nora_goal_untrained_cos: 0.081\n      incommensurable_pairs: 5\n      fair_comparison_pairs: 2\n      openvla_goal_fair_delta: 0.134\n      openvla_spatial_fair_delta: 0.237\n    result_rationale: |\n      D097/D099 修正后，CF sensitivity 的 cross-architecture 对比面临 incommensurability 问题：\n      TracVLA/NORA untrained 无法生成 actions（cosine in hidden space），trained 用 Cohen's d\n      in action space——两个 metrics 不可直接比较。只有 OpenVLA 的 trained + untrained 都能生成\n      actions，可用同一 metric 比较。\n\n      Worst-tier reviewer 攻击：\n      \"CF sensitivity 是你们仅存的两个 training-induced effects 之一（D090 后），但：\n      (1) 你们自己承认 5/7 cross-architecture comparisons 使用 incommensurable metrics（Cohen's d\n      vs cosine distance）。你不能 claim 'training amplifies CF sensitivity' 如果 trained 和\n      untrained 用不同 metrics 测量——这不是 methodological nuance，这是 fundamental flaw。\n      (2) 唯一公平对比（OpenVLA Goal/Spatial）显示 Δ=+0.13/+0.24，即 trained 比 untrained\n      高 12%/25%。但 OpenVLA untrained 是 OXE-pretrained VLA（已有 strong CF d=1.048），\n      所以 'training amplification' 是 VLA→VLA marginal improvement 而非 VLM→VLA dramatic change。\n      (3) 'Empty instruction produces largest deviation' 在 6/8 settings——这不需要 VLA-specific\n      routing 来解释。任何 conditioned generative model 在 input 被完全移除时 output 会 change most。\n      这是 conditioning 的 definition 而非 routing mechanism。\n      (4) CF sensitivity 没有 behavioral grounding：output changes（d=0.65-1.5）是否\n      导致 task failure？如果 perturbed instructions 产生 different but equally valid actions，\n      CF sensitivity 不是 routing evidence 而是 representational noise。\n      缺少 behavioral validation（closed-loop success rate under perturbation）是 near-fatal\n      for CoRL submission。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"CF Sensitivity: Incommensurability Problem\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Trained Metric\", \"Untrained Metric\", \"Comparable?\", \"Fair Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Goal\", \"d=1.182\", \"d=1.048\", \"Yes\", \"+0.134 (12%)\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"d=1.173\", \"d=0.936\", \"Yes\", \"+0.237 (25%)\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Goal\", \"d=1.524\", \"cos=0.153\", \"No\", \"Incommensurable\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"d=1.333\", \"cos=0.180\", \"No\", \"Incommensurable\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Object\", \"d=1.212\", \"cos=0.185\", \"No\", \"Incommensurable\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Long\", \"d=1.473\", \"cos=0.173\", \"No\", \"Incommensurable\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Goal\", \"cos=1.0 (sat.)\", \"cos=0.081\", \"Partially\", \"Saturated — ceiling artifact?\"]\n      - title: \"CF Sensitivity: Missing Behavioral Validation\"\n        columns: [\"What CF Shows\", \"What Reviewer Wants\", \"Gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Output direction changes (d>0.5)\", \"Task success rate drops\", \"No closed-loop data\"]\n          - [\"Empty > wrong > shuffled > para\", \"Perturbation severity → failure rate correlation\", \"No behavioral grounding\"]\n          - [\"ΔMSE≈0 vs ground-truth\", \"Action quality under perturbation\", \"MSE≈0 suggests no quality impact\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bars with 5/7 pairs marked 'INCOMMENSURABLE' in red\"\n      - \"ΔMSE≈0 annotated as 'CF changes direction but not quality — no functional consequence'\"\n    analysis: |\n      CF sensitivity 在 worst tier 下被 double-attacked: incommensurable metrics + no behavioral\n      grounding。ΔMSE≈0 (ground-truth error unchanged under ablation) is particularly damaging——\n      it suggests CF perturbation changes output direction without degrading quality，\n      supporting \"information-computation dissociation\" (Hewitt & Liang 2019) interpretation\n      that routing modulates output but doesn't encode task-critical information。\n      Framework reframe：CF analysis 降为 \"framework's perturbation analysis capability\"，\n      behavioral validation 列为 \"critical future work\"。\n\n  - name: \"Three-Tier Routing Gradient (D094)\"\n    plan_id: \"three_tier_gradient\"\n    description: \"VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA → task-finetuned VLA 三层级路由梯度\"\n    expected_results:\n      tier1_models: [\"Phi-3-Vision\", \"Qwen2.5-VL\", \"random init Llama-2\"]\n      tier1_l1_heads: [32, 14, 0]\n      tier1_cf_max_cos: 0.19\n      tier1_exit_collapse: false\n      tier2_model: \"openvla-7b (OXE)\"\n      tier2_l1_heads: 25\n      tier2_cf_d: 1.048\n      tier2_exit_collapse: false\n      tier3_l1_heads: [24, 30, 13]\n      tier3_exit_collapse_vlm_origin: true\n      tier3_exit_collapse_vla_origin: false\n      tier2_n_datapoints: 1\n    result_rationale: |\n      三层级梯度被 worst reviewer 驳为 post-hoc narrative with N=1 at Tier-2。\n      \n      攻击 1 — 统计力不足：\"Tier-2 只有一个数据点（openvla-7b OXE pretrained）。要建立 gradient\n      你需要 at minimum 3 个独立的 OXE-pretrained 或 general-pretrained VLA checkpoints 来\n      验证 Tier-2 不是 openvla-7b specific。Three points don't make a gradient if the middle\n      one is N=1——那是 step function with one interpolation point。\"\n      \n      攻击 2 — L1 heads 在 tiers 间不单调：\"Tier-1 Phi-3-Vision = 32/32, Tier-2 OXE = 25/32,\n      Tier-3 TracVLA = 27-30/32。Tier-1 > Tier-2 ≈ Tier-3——这不是 gradient，这是 'base model\n      already saturated then training reduces some heads'。L1 head count 不支持 gradient narrative。\"\n      \n      攻击 3 — Exit collapse 不支持 gradient：\"Tier-2 无 exit collapse, Tier-3 有 exit collapse\n      只在 VLM→VLA origin models——这是 binary transition 不是 gradient。如果 Tier-3 只在\n      VLM-origin 有 collapse 而 VLA-origin 没有，那 'gradient' 应该有 collapse 强度在 Tier-2→Tier-3\n      increasing——但 Tier-2 = 0, Tier-3 (VLA origin) = 0。只有 Tier-3 (VLM origin) 有 collapse。\n      这是 binary (VLM→VLA collapse exists / doesn't) 不是 three-tier gradient。\"\n      \n      攻击 4 — libero_finetuned attention data 反驳 gradient：\"L31 exit engagement 从 bridge-VLA\n      (18 heads) 到 libero-finetuned (0 heads)——further specialization REDUCES exit routing。\n      Gradient predicts 'more training = more routing' 但 data shows opposite at exit layer。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Three-Tier Gradient: N=1 at Tier-2\"\n        columns: [\"Tier\", \"N Models\", \"Key Metrics\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Tier 1 (VLM)\", \"3+\", \"L1: 0-32; CF<0.2; no collapse\", \"Adequate N but heterogeneous (0 vs 32 heads)\"]\n          - [\"Tier 2 (General VLA)\", \"1 ONLY\", \"L1: 25; CF d=1.05; no collapse\", \"N=1 — cannot establish gradient\"]\n          - [\"Tier 3 (Task VLA)\", \"~10 cells\", \"L1: 13-30; CF d>0.45; collapse if VLM-origin\", \"Adequate N but split by origin\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Gradient diagram with Tier-2 marked 'N=1' and dashed connections\"\n      - \"L1 head count across tiers showing non-monotonic pattern (Phi-3: 32→25→30)\"\n    analysis: |\n      Three-tier gradient 必须移除或降为 \"preliminary observation with N=1 at intermediate tier\"。\n      Framework reframe：不 claim gradient，改为 \"framework enables stage-wise comparison\"——\n      contribute methodology for comparing training stages, not the gradient finding itself.\n\n  - name: \"NLP Finetuning Control (D100)\"\n    plan_id: \"nlp_finetuning_control\"\n    description: \"Llama-2-7b-chat R² profile 排除 generic fine-tuning confound\"\n    expected_results:\n      peak_r2: 0.1555\n      exit_r2: 0.1555\n      delta_r2: 0.000\n      profile_shape: \"flat constant across all 32 layers\"\n      r2_range: [0.1547, 0.1555]\n      phi3_nlp_delta: 0.000\n      qwen_nlp_delta: 0.000\n    result_rationale: |\n      D100 结果 clean：三个 NLP-finetuned LLM（Llama-2-chat, Phi-3-instruct, Qwen2.5-instruct）\n      均 ΔR²=0.000，flat R²≈0.155 noise floor。这排除了 \"exit collapse is generic fine-tuning artifact\"。\n\n      但 worst-tier reviewer 不被 impressed：\n      \"D100 是 good negative control，我们接受 exit collapse 不是 generic fine-tuning。\n      但这不能 elevate exit collapse 为 interesting finding——它只从 'might be generic artifact'\n      升级为 'VLA-specific but trivially expected'。当你训练一个 language model 来 predict\n      7-DOF robot actions，exit layer 表征当然会被 action training reshape。\n      R²≈0.155 in NLP models 只是说明 NLP models 没有 action-relevant information 在任何层\n      （Ridge 只拟合 between-task variance）——当然不会有 exit collapse。\n      你排除了一个 straw-man confound 但没有建立 positive value。\n      A good control experiment answers 'is this finding real?' — yours answers 'is this finding\n      even more trivially explainable than I thought?'  答案是 No，但 the finding is still trivial。\"\n\n      R²=0.155 本身是 between-task variance baseline（10 tasks → Ridge 可拟合 task identity → \n      0.155 R² from 10-way between-task variance alone）——这是 expected 而非 surprising。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"NLP Finetuning Control Results\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Backbone\", \"ΔR²\", \"Profile\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Llama-2-7b-chat\", \"Llama-2-7B\", \"0.000\", \"Flat 0.155\", \"Expected: no action info anywhere\"]\n          - [\"Phi-3-mini-instruct\", \"Phi-3-mini\", \"0.000\", \"Flat 0.155\", \"Expected: same noise floor\"]\n          - [\"Qwen2.5-3B-instruct\", \"Qwen2.5-3B\", \"0.000\", \"Flat 0.155\", \"Expected: same noise floor\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA (TracVLA)\", \"Phi-3-mini\", \"0.156-0.294\", \"Exit collapse\", \"VLA-specific but trivially expected\"]\n          - [\"VLA→VLA (OpenVLA)\", \"Llama-2-7B\", \"0.033-0.086\", \"Mild decline\", \"No new collapse in VLA→VLA\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer R² with NLP controls as flat lines at 0.155 — 'straw-man excluded' annotation\"\n    analysis: |\n      D100 是 necessary but not sufficient defense。Worst reviewer accepts the control\n      but doesn't give credit for it — \"excluding an obvious confound is minimum bar,\n      not contribution.\" Framework reframe 可以 cite D100 作为 \"framework enables\n      cross-domain comparison\" demo，但 reviewer 的 next-level attack（trivially expected）\n      仍 stands。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Instruction Classification (C1 Framework)\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_instruction_classification\"\n    description: \"10-way instruction classification 跨层 × 跨条件 — C1 框架核心实验\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_L1_acc: 0.996\n      trained_L2_to_L31: 1.000\n      llama2base_L1_acc: 0.802\n      llama2base_L5_plus: 1.000\n      untrained_L1_acc: 1.000\n      untrained_L31_acc: 0.820\n      image_mean_all_layers: 0.10\n      loocv_trained: \"100.00±0.00\"\n      loocv_untrained: \"84.76±11.59\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据完整。Worst 档下 C1 被彻底降级：\n      \"10-way classification on 4096-dim features 是 trivially easy。Untrained (random init)\n      L1 也达到 100%——random projection 就能分离 10 个 class。你的 LOOCV 只在 untrained deep layers\n      下降到 85%——这不是 'training improves routing' 而是 'random weights corrupt signal in deep layers'。\n      \n      Image mean = 10% at all layers 是 causal mask guarantee 不是 finding。你自己承认了。\n      \n      三条件对比（trained flat 100%, llama2base saturates L5, untrained decays to 82%）的\n      interpretation 也被质疑：'trained L1=99.6% vs llama2base L1=80.2%' 看起来像 'training\n      creates immediate routing'，但 D090 证明 L1 heads 来自 base model 而非 training。\n      那 99.6% vs 80.2% 的差异可能只反映 VLA fine-tuning 后 feature quality 提升（action-relevant\n      features are more linearly separable）而非 routing reorganization。\n      \n      贡献在 methodology（factorial design + 4 methods）而非 findings。但 methodology 贡献在\n      CoRL 通常只值 weak accept——CoRL 偏好 systems + behavioral results。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Instruction Classification: Trivially Easy?\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"L1 Acc\", \"L31 Acc\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained\", \"99.6%\", \"100%\", \"Flat 100% = ceiling effect, no gradient to analyze\"]\n          - [\"Llama-2 base\", \"80.2%\", \"100%\", \"LM pretraining provides separability, not VLA training\"]\n          - [\"Untrained (random)\", \"100%\", \"82%\", \"Even random features separate 10 classes at L1\"]\n          - [\"Image mean\", \"10%\", \"10%\", \"Causal mask guarantee, not finding\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-condition probe curves annotated with 'trivially easy' at ceiling regions\"\n    analysis: |\n      C1 的 experimental framework 是 reframe 后的 primary contribution。但 cross-instruction\n      classification 作为 framework demo 的问题：10-way on 4096d 太 easy，不 demonstrate\n      framework 在 harder settings 下的 value。需要更 challenging classification tasks\n      或 fine-grained metrics 来 justify framework utility。\n\n  - name: \"Head Ablation and Specificity Controls\"\n    plan_id: \"head_ablation_suite\"\n    description: \"L1 attention head ablation 实验套件 — 验证 instruction-dominant heads 的功能特异性\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_r2_L13: 0.676\n      ablate_24_instr_r2_L13: 0.676\n      ablate_24_random_r2_L13: 0.664\n      random_24_z_score: -2.73\n      specificity_ratio: 1.08\n      instruction_d: 0.651\n      random_24_d: 0.601\n      image_24_d: 0.580\n      gt_error_delta_mse: -0.001\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据已完成。Worst 档下 ablation 结果被严厉解读：\n      \n      (1) Specificity ratio = 1.08x 极弱：\"instruction-dominant 24 heads 的 per-head effect\n      不比 random 24 heads 大多少（z=-2.73 但 effect size tiny）。任何 24/32 heads ablation\n      产生 similar or larger R² increase（random 24 mean delta = 0.077 > instruction 24 delta = 0.042）。\n      Instruction-dominant heads 不是 special——they're 75% of all heads，removing ANY 75%\n      of heads produces similar effects。\"\n      \n      (2) ΔMSE≈0 vs ground-truth 是 worst tier 最致命的 finding：\"你 ablate 24 instruction-dominant\n      heads，action outputs change direction (d=0.65) 但 ground-truth error 不变（ΔMSE=-0.001, p=0.52）。\n      这意味着 instruction routing 对 action quality 无影响——perturbation 改变 output 方向\n      但不改变 output 质量。这直接证明 CF sensitivity 缺乏 functional significance。\n      如果移除 75% 的 'instruction routing heads' 对 action quality 无影响，\n      那 instruction routing 在 action generation 中可能是 redundant mechanism。\"\n      \n      (3) Information-computation dissociation 解读在 worst tier 下被反转：论文 cite Hewitt & Liang 2019\n      作为 \"ΔMSE≈0 is expected under dissociation\"，但 reviewer 说：\n      \"Hewitt & Liang 的 point 是 probe results don't prove representation is functionally used。\n      你在用他们的 framework 来 excuse 你的 negative result。ΔMSE≈0 doesn't support 'routing\n      modulates without degrading'——it supports 'routing doesn't matter for output quality'。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Head Ablation: No Functional Specificity\"\n        columns: [\"Ablation Group\", \"24h d\", \"Per-head d\", \"GT ΔMSE\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Instr-dominant 24\", \"0.651\", \"0.027\", \"-0.001 (p=0.52)\", \"Changes direction, not quality\"]\n          - [\"Random 24 (avg)\", \"0.601\", \"0.025\", \"similar\", \"Any 24 heads produce similar effect\"]\n          - [\"Image-dominant 24\", \"0.580\", \"0.024\", \"similar\", \"No group specificity\"]\n          - [\"Control 8 (random)\", \"0.410\", \"0.051\", \"similar\", \"Per-head effect LARGER in control\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ΔMSE≈0 highlighted as 'no functional consequence of instruction routing ablation'\"\n    analysis: |\n      Head ablation suite is worst tier's most damaging evidence against CF sensitivity as\n      functional routing. ΔMSE≈0 + specificity ratio 1.08x together argue that instruction\n      routing (as measured by attention head dominance) has no disproportionate functional role.\n      Framework reframe 很难 rescue this——the framework's own ablation tool reveals that\n      the effect it detected (instruction routing) is not functionally specific.\n\n  - name: \"Counterfactual Token Overlap and Trajectory-Level Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"cf_detailed_analysis\"\n    description: \"CF perturbation 的 token overlap, trajectory-level d, 和 ΔMSE 扩展分析\"\n    expected_results:\n      token_overlap_spearman: 1.0\n      empty_d_token: 0.968\n      empty_d_trajectory: 3.438\n      wrong_d_token: 0.844\n      wrong_d_trajectory: 3.798\n      shuffled_d_token: 0.625\n      shuffled_d_trajectory: 2.595\n      para_d_token: 0.697\n      para_d_trajectory: 2.131\n      inflation_factor_mean: 0.245\n      gt_mse_original: 0.498\n      gt_mse_top24_ablated: 0.497\n      gt_mse_delta: -0.001\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据已完成。Worst 档下 token overlap analysis 被反过来用：\n      \n      \"Spearman ρ=1.0 between token novelty and Cohen's d 说明 CF sensitivity 完全由\n      lexical/positional distance 驱动，不是 semantic distance。Empty（最大 token novelty）→\n      largest d，shuffled（same tokens, different order）→ moderate d，paraphrased（high overlap）→\n      smallest d。这不是 'the model understands instruction semantics'——这是 'the model responds\n      to surface-level token changes'。任何 autoregressive language model 都会如此。\"\n      \n      Trajectory-level d（2.1-3.8）远大于 token-level d（0.6-0.97）——inflation factor ~4x。\n      Worst reviewer：\"trajectory-level inflation 说明 per-timestep effects 累积——这不是\n      'stronger evidence of routing' 而是 'autocorrelation amplification'。每个 timestep\n      的小 perturbation 通过 temporal autocorrelation 累积成大 trajectory difference，\n      这是 dynamical systems 的 trivial property 不是 routing evidence。\"\n      \n      GT MSE unchanged（0.498 vs 0.497）再次确认 CF perturbation 不影响 action quality。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Token Overlap → Cohen's d: Surface-Level Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"Token Novelty\", \"Token d\", \"Traj d\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"empty\", \"1.0\", \"0.968\", \"3.438\", \"Max novelty → max effect: lexical, not semantic\"]\n          - [\"wrong\", \"0.83\", \"0.844\", \"3.798\", \"High novelty → high effect\"]\n          - [\"paraphrased\", \"0.47\", \"0.697\", \"2.131\", \"Low novelty → low effect\"]\n          - [\"shuffled\", \"0.0\", \"0.625\", \"2.595\", \"Zero novelty but positional change → moderate\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Token novelty vs d scatter with ρ=1.0 line — annotated 'surface-level sensitivity, not semantic routing'\"\n    analysis: |\n      ρ=1.0 token-novelty/d correlation is worst-tier's strongest argument that CF sensitivity\n      measures lexical sensitivity rather than semantic routing. Framework reframe has no good\n      counter — the framework's own analysis reveals CF is surface-level. Could argue \"shuffled\n      same tokens different order still produces d=0.63\" as evidence of positional sensitivity\n      beyond pure lexical, but this is weak defense.\n\n  - name: \"D090 Synthesis: What VLA Training Actually Contributes\"\n    plan_id: \"d090_contribution_synthesis\"\n    description: \"综合评估：D090 后论文的 residual contribution\"\n    expected_results:\n      training_induced_effects: [\"R² exit collapse (VLM→VLA only)\", \"CF sensitivity (unfair baselines)\"]\n      base_model_effects: [\"L1 head count\", \"deep-layer probe stability\"]\n      removed_contributions: [\"L1 routing gradient\", \"attention bookend pattern (entry component)\"]\n      remaining_unique: \"1-2 effects, both with caveats\"\n      reviewer_avg_score: [4.0, 5.5]\n      strong_reject_count: [1, 2]\n      accept_probability: [0.05, 0.20]\n      claims_surviving: [0.5, 1.5]\n    result_rationale: |\n      D090 后 contribution audit 在 worst tier 下：\n      \n      Training-induced（retained but weakened）:\n      - R² exit collapse：6/6 VLM→VLA, 0/4 VLA→VLA — clean binary。D100 排除 NLP confound。\n        但 worst reviewer 视为 \"trivially expected transition artifact\"。\n      - CF sensitivity：d≥0.45 in all trained settings。但 incommensurable baselines（5/7 pairs），\n        ρ=1.0 token-novelty correlation（surface-level），ΔMSE≈0（no functional consequence）。\n      \n      Base-model-dependent（removed from contribution）:\n      - L1 head count：Phi-3 32/32 untrained, NORA 13/16 untrained — not training-induced。\n      - Deep-layer stability：Llama-2 base also stable（100% L5+）— from LM pretraining。\n      \n      Reviewer score prediction:\n      - R1（expects behavioral results）：4/10 — \"descriptive analysis without actionable insight,\n        CoRL expects at minimum open-loop policy evaluation.\"\n      - R2（appreciates methodology）：6/10 — \"framework is solid and systematic, cross-architecture\n        validation is thorough engineering. But findings are thin after D090 self-critique.\"\n      - R3（generalizability focus）：4/10 — \"exit collapse magnitude 4.4x range within VLM→VLA,\n        CF baselines incommensurable. Claims are over-qualified to the point of being unfalsifiable.\"\n      Mean: 4.67. Strong reject: 0-1. Accept probability: 0.10-0.20.\n      \n      Reframe 能做的最大提升：如果 C1 framework 成功 pitch 为 primary contribution（\"first\n      systematic VLA profiling toolkit\"），R2 可能升到 7，但 R1/R3 不变——\n      结果 mean 5.0，borderline reject。需要 AC 同情才有机会。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Worst-Tier Score Prediction\"\n        columns: [\"Reviewer\", \"Score\", \"Primary Concern\", \"Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"R1 (behavioral)\", \"4\", \"No closed-loop validation; CoRL is robotics venue\", \"Reject\"]\n          - [\"R2 (methodology)\", \"6\", \"Framework solid; findings thin but honest\", \"Weak Accept\"]\n          - [\"R3 (generalizability)\", \"4\", \"Magnitude variance; incommensurable baselines; over-qualified claims\", \"Reject\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"4.67\", \"2 reject + 1 weak accept\", \"Likely Reject\"]\n      - title: \"Reframe Impact on Scores\"\n        columns: [\"Reframe Element\", \"Score Impact\", \"Which Reviewer\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"C1 framework as primary contribution\", \"+1 for R2 only\", \"R2: 6→7\"]\n          - [\"D090 as framework capability demo\", \"+0.5 for R2\", \"R2 already sympathetic\"]\n          - [\"Exit collapse as diagnostic\", \"0 for R1/R3\", \"Doesn't address behavioral gap\"]\n          - [\"Roadmap for closed-loop future work\", \"+0.5 for R1 maybe\", \"R1 may soften to 4.5\"]\n          - [\"Net after reframe\", \"Mean ~5.0\", \"Still borderline reject\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Contribution pyramid after D090: framework base (solid), exit collapse (thin), CF (thin), L1 routing (crossed out)\"\n    analysis: |\n      Worst tier 核心判定：论文 honest analysis (D090) + thorough controls (D100) 是 scientifically\n      commendable 但 strategically devastating。每个 defense 实验排除了一个 confound 但同时削弱了\n      contribution scope。D090 证明 L1 routing 不是训练效果；D100 证明 exit collapse 不是 generic\n      finetuning 但仍被视为 trivial；ΔMSE≈0 证明 ablation 不影响 quality 但被解读为 \"routing\n      doesn't functionally matter\"。\n      \n      Reframe 路径：diagnostic framework + honest empirical characterization。Accept probability\n      0.05-0.20 range。需要 AC 认可 methodology contribution 的 standalone value 才有机会。\n      关键 rebuttal material：(1) representation engineering literature 论证 representational\n      analysis 的独立价值，(2) exit collapse as VLM→VLA binary diagnostic 的 concrete use case\n      （判断 pretraining checkpoint 是否完成 VLA transition），(3) framework reusability 的\n      具体 demonstration（how others can apply it to new VLAs）。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24097,"cache_read_input_tokens":67106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24097},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4327d556-6a05-42fb-ae30-82d4a0777322","uuid":"9f41727a-7b18-4e6a-a016-1b51e819edb1"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":506334,"duration_api_ms":507566,"num_turns":3,"result":"Now I have the complete picture. Let me generate the full worst-tier predictions based on the updated D096/D099/D100/D102 findings and the actual registry data.\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Reviewers 认为 exit collapse 是 trivially expected（VLM→VLA 当然改变表征），CF 无 behavioral grounding 缺乏 functional significance，\n  论文被视为 descriptive analysis without actionable insight。D100 NLP control（Llama-2-chat ΔR²=0.000）虽然排除了 generic fine-tuning\n  confound，但 worst-tier reviewer 将此重新解读为：\"好，exit collapse 不是 generic fine-tuning 的——但它仍然是 trivially expected\n  的 VLM→VLA transition effect。当你把 language model 改造成 action model，出口层表征当然会重组——这不需要你的 framework 来'发现'。\"\n  D102 的 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 二元分离被反过来论证：\"你自己证明了 exit collapse 是 one-time transition artifact，不是 ongoing\n  routing mechanism。它在 VLA→VLA finetuning 时消失（0/4），说明它不是 functional routing signature 而是 initial adaptation shock。\n  这反而削弱了 exit collapse 作为 'diagnostic tool' 的价值——它只能告诉你 '这个模型曾经从 VLM 变成 VLA'，这在实践中谁不知道？\"\n  Reframe 方向：从 \"discovering routing mechanisms\" 转为 \"diagnostic methodology for VLA development\"。核心 pitch 变为：\n  本文提供第一个系统化的 VLA representational profiling toolkit，跨 3 架构验证。但 worst-tier 下即使此 reframe 也被质疑：\n  \"一个 diagnostic framework 如果主要发现是 trivially expected（exit collapse）和 functionally unvalidated（CF sensitivity），\n  那 framework 的 utility 在哪里？你需要 demonstrate 这个 framework 能发现 non-obvious actionable insights。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"SigLIP+Projector RSA 对比 Full VLA 和 DINO，证明 action-relevant 结构源自 frozen vision encoder\"\n    expected_results:\n      siglip_projector_rsa: 0.615\n      trained_with_inst_rsa: 0.488\n      untrained_with_inst_rsa: 0.485\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      llm_degradation_delta: 0.127\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据已完成不变。在 worst 档下，此实验仅覆盖 OpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP encoder。Reviewer 攻击路线：\n      \"SigLIP+Projector RSA=0.615 是 OpenVLA-specific frozen encoder 的观察。TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision encoder，\n      NORA 用 InternViT——你们没测这些 encoder 的 RSA。单架构 encoder analysis 无法 claim architecture-independent。\"\n      LLM degradation（0.615→0.488）本身被视为 \"trivially expected—— LLM 的 intermediate processing 当然会\n      改变 representation geometry，这不是 finding 而是 definition。\" 在 diagnostic framework reframe 下，\n      此实验降为 \"framework 在 OpenVLA 上的 case study\"——不再是 core contribution。更致命的是，Reviewer 会用\n      这个实验反过来攻击论文 motivation：\"如果 frozen encoder 已经提供了最好的 action-relevant structure（RSA=0.615），\n      而 LLM processing 只是 degrade 它（到 0.488），那为什么要研究 LLM 内部的 instruction routing？问题不在 routing\n      而在 LLM 设计本身——你应该研究如何让 LLM 不 degrade encoder output。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SigLIP RSA Scope Limitation (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"RSA\", \"Architecture Coverage\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SigLIP+Proj\", \"0.615\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Cannot generalize to other VLA encoders\"]\n          - [\"VLA trained\", \"0.488\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Llama-2-specific LLM degradation\"]\n          - [\"VLA untrained\", \"0.485\", \"OpenVLA only\", \"Random-init Llama-2 specific\"]\n          - [\"DINO\", \"0.388\", \"Standalone\", \"Reference baseline, unaffected\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart 标注 'OpenVLA only' 在每个 bar 上方，突显 single-arch limitation\"\n    analysis: |\n      Framework reframe 下此实验从 C1 core evidence 降为 Section 4.1 case study。价值在于 demonstrate\n      framework 的 encoder-LLM decomposition 能力，而非 claim 本身。Reviewer 不会因此给分但也不会因此扣分——\n      neutral contribution in worst tier。但 LLM degradation finding 可能被用来攻击论文 motivation 本身。\n\n  - name: \"DINO baseline RSA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"Standalone vision model 参照基线\"\n    expected_results:\n      dino_rsa: 0.388\n      dino_action_R2: 0.687\n      dino_subtask_auc: 0.972\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。Worst 档下 DINO 的角色被 weaponize：R²=0.687 对比 VLA 训练后的 exit R² drop。Reviewer：\n      \"DINO（self-supervised, 无 language, 无 action training）的 action probe R²=0.687 已经很高，\n      说明 action prediction 主要是 visual task。你们声称的 VLA 训练重组 instruction routing，但如果一个\n      纯视觉模型无需任何 instruction 就能达到 R²=0.687，instruction routing 的 practical value 是什么？\n      这反而证明了 Grant et al. 2026 的 visual dominance finding——instructions 在 VLA 中可能根本不重要。\"\n      DINO subtask AUC=0.972 进一步强化这个论点——task progress 几乎完全可从 visual features 预测，\n      无需 instruction information。这直接攻击论文研究 instruction routing 的 premise。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"DINO R²=0.687 标注在所有 cross-arch R² exit collapse 图上作为 'no-language baseline'\"\n    analysis: |\n      Worst tier 下 DINO baseline 被用来论证整篇论文的 premise 可疑：如果 vision alone 足够好，\n      instruction routing research 的 practical relevance 被严重削弱。Framework reframe 可以\n      acknowledge 但无法完全化解这个攻击。\n\n  - name: \"Per-layer RSA degradation curve\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹\"\n    expected_results:\n      proj_rsa: 0.615\n      trained_peak_rsa: 0.488\n      trained_peak_layer: 9\n      untrained_peak_rsa: 0.485\n      untrained_peak_layer: 12\n      proj_to_l1_drop: 0.13\n      inverted_u_trained: true\n      inverted_u_untrained: true\n      rise_phase_delta: 0.016\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。Worst 档下 inverted-U 只在 OpenVLA (Llama-2) 上验证过，TracVLA/NORA 的 RSA per-layer\n      curve 从未做过。CKA 在 plan_009 中反转了 RSA ordering（untrained > trained），使 RSA metric 的\n      authority 受损。Rise phase Δρ=0.016 极小（CI 可能 includes 0），reviewer 会指出：\n      \"你声称 training shifts RSA peak from L0 to L12，但 rise phase 只有 0.016 ρ——这在 noise level 内。\n      如果 CKA 不支持 inverted-U，你不能 claim 这是 robust pattern——这是 metric-specific artifact。\"\n      在 CoRL（robotics venue），per-layer RSA curve 被视为 \"interesting visualization but not\n      contribution\"——reviewer 期望功能性验证而非几何观察。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RSA Inverted-U Architecture Coverage\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"RSA Per-Layer Done?\", \"Pattern\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B)\", \"Yes\", \"Inverted-U\", \"Only confirmed case, CKA reversal undermines\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA (Phi-3-mini)\", \"No\", \"Unknown\", \"Cannot claim generalization\"]\n          - [\"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)\", \"No\", \"Unknown\", \"Cannot claim generalization\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer RSA curve 只有 OpenVLA 一条线，旁注 'CKA reversal: untrained > trained'\"\n    analysis: |\n      Inverted-U 成为 C3 observation 的核心证据但被 metric-dependence 严重削弱。\n      Framework reframe 下可保留为 \"framework reveals metric-dependent patterns\"\n      但这同时 undermine 了 framework 发现的 authority——如果换个 metric 结论就变，framework 的可靠性如何？\n\n  - name: \"Output head analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"SigLIP+projector frozen 确认, LLM 权重变化不传导到表征\"\n    expected_results:\n      vision_projector_cos_sim: 1.0\n      llm_rel_change_mean: 1.316\n      llm_rel_change_range: [1.22, 1.37]\n      head_vs_llm_ratio: 1.12\n      shallow_adaptation_gate: \"FAIL\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。Worst 档下此实验被视为 trivial verification：\"OpenVLA 代码 freeze 了 vision encoder，\n      你只是验证了代码做了它该做的事。cos_sim=1.0 不是 finding，是 implementation check。\"\n      LLM 权重均匀分布（1.22-1.37）也不 surprising——\"random init vs pretrained 的差异当然大且均匀，\n      这是 comparing random weights to structured weights，不是 analyzing fine-tuning effects。\n      你的 caveat 自己也说了：comparison is pretrained Llama + fine-tune vs random init，\n      所以 differences dominated by pretrained vs random，not by VLA training.\"\n      在 8-page limit 下，worst tier 建议此实验压缩为半段或移到 appendix。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      贡献接近零。Framework reframe 下可作为 \"component attribution capability\" 的 one-sentence\n      mention。不值得独立分析。\n\n  - name: \"6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks 系统验证\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained 表征结构\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_untrained_rsa_delta: 0.003\n      trained_untrained_r2_delta: 0.015\n      cka_ordering_reversal: true\n      all_methods_show_vla_gt_dino: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Orphaned 但子实验（RSA, R², CKA, action probe, delta probe, classification）均已完成。\n      Worst 档下 trained ≈ untrained 被视为 \"trivially expected under frozen encoder\"。\n      Reviewer：\"frozen SigLIP+projector 输出相同 L0 features，LLM fine-tuning 只改变 weights\n      而非 input distribution——所以 intermediate layer representations naturally similar。\n      你用 6 种方法验证一个 structurally guaranteed result，这不是 thoroughness 而是 over-verification。\"\n      CKA ordering reversal 进一步削弱 multi-method consistency narrative——6 methods 中 CKA\n      反转了 RSA，说明 \"consistency\" 是 cherry-picked（只 consistent 在某些 metrics 下）。\n      Worst reviewer 总结：\"这些实验证明了 VLA > DINO 但 trained ≈ untrained——\n      前者 expected（LLM 有 4096d features vs DINO 1024d），后者 也 expected（same encoder）。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"6 Methods Under Worst-Tier Reinterpretation\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Trained-Untrained Δ\", \"Worst Reviewer Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA (geometric)\", \"0.003\", \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"]\n          - [\"R² action probe\", \"+0.015\", \"Marginal: within noise\"]\n          - [\"CKA (global)\", \"-0.006\", \"REVERSAL: undermines RSA narrative\"]\n          - [\"Action probe (MLP)\", \"+0.045\", \"Small routing effect, not surprising\"]\n          - [\"Delta probe\", \"+0.011\", \"Same encoder → similar structure\"]\n          - [\"Classification\", \"+0.001\", \"Trivially easy for both conditions\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"6-method consistency radar chart 标注 'CKA reversal' 打破 perfect consistency 叙事\"\n    analysis: |\n      6 methods consistency 从 \"strong evidence for trained ≈ untrained\" 降为\n      \"thorough but unsurprising verification of a structurally predicted outcome\"。\n      CKA reversal 使 \"all methods consistent\" claim 不成立。Framework reframe 下\n      唯一残余价值：demonstrate framework 的 multi-method coverage capability。\n\n  - name: \"Instruction ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\"\n    expected_results:\n      delta_with_vs_no_inst: 0.004\n      gate_judgment: \"FAIL — instruction 无影响 on RSA\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。Worst 档下被视为 tautological sanity check：image token RSA 在 causal mask 下\n      不受 instruction tokens 影响是 structural guarantee，不是 empirical finding。\n      Reviewer：\"你在 C1 里承认 causal mask 使 image tokens 看不到 instructions，\n      然后在 plan_006 里'发现' image RSA 不受 instructions 影响——这是验证了你自己的前提假设。\n      Δ=0.004 是 noise，不是 small effect——effect 在结构上不可能存在。\n      这 0.5 页可以省掉或用一句话带过。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Worst tier 下从 C3 evidence 降为 \"confirms structural prediction, not finding\"。\n      Framework reframe 下可作为 \"sanity check\" 一句带过，不占独立段落。\n\n  - name: \"2×2 matrix (training × instruction)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"四条件全收敛验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_with_inst: 0.488\n      trained_no_inst: 0.489\n      untrained_with_inst: 0.485\n      untrained_no_inst: 0.480\n      bootstrap_ci_includes_0: true\n      training_effect: 0.003\n      instruction_effect: 0.004\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。Worst 档下 2×2 null result 被视为 \"expected outcome of frozen encoder + causal mask\"。\n      Reviewer：\"你的 2×2 factorial design 是好的 experimental methodology，但它发现了 predicted null——\n      both factors (training, instruction) have no effect on image token RSA 因为 (1) encoder frozen,\n      (2) causal mask blocks instruction→image. 好的 experimental design + expected null result\n      = methodology paper contribution, not empirical contribution。如果这是 methodology paper\n      那 ok，但你 pitch 的是 empirical findings about VLA routing。\"\n      四条件收敛到 0.48-0.49 band 进一步证实 RSA 对 image tokens 是 ceiling+floor bounded by encoder quality。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 Matrix as Expected Null (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"RSA\", \"Reviewer Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained + Inst\", \"0.488\", \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"]\n          - [\"Trained - Inst\", \"0.489\", \"Expected: causal mask blocks\"]\n          - [\"Untrained + Inst\", \"0.485\", \"Expected: same encoder\"]\n          - [\"Untrained - Inst\", \"0.480\", \"Expected: both factors null\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 heatmap 标注 'Predicted null under frozen encoder hypothesis'\"\n    analysis: |\n      Framework reframe 下 2×2 matrix 的价值从 \"finding\" 转为 \"exemplar of factorial\n      design capability\"——可复用性贡献，但在 CoRL 不计高分。\n\n  - name: \"Random instruction control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"随机/无意义 instruction 替代验证 RSA 不受 instruction content 影响\"\n    expected_results:\n      normal_rsa: 0.489\n      random_rsa: 0.484\n      shuffled_rsa: 0.483\n      empty_rsa: 0.472\n      max_absolute_delta: 0.017\n      instruction_invariant: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。与 plan_006/007 同一逻辑链——causal mask 使 image token RSA 对 instruction content\n      天然不变。Worst reviewer：\"你用了三个 experiments（006/007/008）验证同一个 structurally guaranteed\n      null result。Normal/random/shuffled/empty 全在 ±0.02 内不是 finding，是 noise around a\n      guaranteed null。这占了论文篇幅但不增加 contribution。在 8 页限制下，三个实验应压缩为 1 段 sanity check。\"\n      更刻薄的 reviewer：\"spending 3 experiments on 'image tokens don't see instruction tokens'\n      suggests the authors don't fully understand their own architecture's causal mask structure.\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      006/007/008 三合一压缩为半段。Framework reframe 下仅作为 \"invariance verification\"\n      methodology demo。在 worst tier 下浪费篇幅的风险 > 贡献。\n\n  - name: \"CKA verification\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"CKA 指标验证 RSA 发现的 metric robustness\"\n    expected_results:\n      linear_cka_ordering: \"untrained > trained > projector > DINO\"\n      rsa_ordering: \"projector > trained > untrained > DINO\"\n      ordering_reversal: true\n      last_preaction_cka: 0.127\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。CKA-RSA dissociation 在 worst 档下变得 doubly 致命。\n      第一层攻击（保持不变）：\"如果 CKA 说 untrained > trained 而 RSA 说 trained > untrained，\n      那哪个 metric 才反映 'action-relevant information'？你选了 RSA 来讲 story，但另一个\n      equally principled metric 给出相反结论。这不是 metric dissociation finding——\n      这是 your conclusions are metric-dependent 的 admission。\"\n      第二层攻击（D095 升级后更致命）：\"你们现在 claim R² exit collapse 是跨架构一致的\n      VLM→VLA signature。但 R² 本身是 functional metric（probe-based），RSA 是 geometric metric，\n      CKA 是 kernel-based metric。如果不同 metrics 给不同结论，你凭什么用 R² 的 exit collapse\n      而不是 CKA 的 no-collapse 来 claim 'architecture-independent signature'？\n      你的 framework 应该 reconcile 这些 metrics 而不是 pick 对你有利的那个。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Metric Ordering Reversal (Worst-Tier Authority Crisis)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Ordering\", \"Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"RSA (geometric)\", \"SigLIP > T > U > DINO\", \"Training degrades geometry\"]\n          - [\"CKA (global)\", \"U > T > SigLIP > DINO\", \"Training preserves/improves structure\"]\n          - [\"R² (functional)\", \"T_lastpre > DINO ≈ Proj > T_img > U\", \"Training enables routing\"]\n          - [\"Reviewer question\", \"—\", \"Framework credibility if metrics disagree?\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Triple ordering diagram 标注 contradiction arrows between RSA and CKA\"\n    analysis: |\n      CKA dissociation 在 worst tier 下是 double-edged：可以包装为 \"why we need multi-metric\n      framework\" 但同时 undermines 所有 single-metric conclusions。Exit collapse 只在 R²\n      下明显——如果 CKA 下不 collapse，reviewer 要求 \"architecture-independent\" 必须\n      \"metric-independent\"，否则 claim 降级。\n\n  - name: \"LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark 扩展\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"第三个 benchmark（LIBERO-Spatial）交叉验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.696\n      trained_image_mean_peak_layer: 13\n      trained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.675\n      trained_last_preaction_peak_layer: 21\n      untrained_image_mean_peak_R2: 0.673\n      untrained_last_preaction_peak_R2: 0.635\n      trained_vs_untrained_delta_imgmean: 0.023\n      trained_vs_untrained_delta_lastpre: 0.040\n      bootstrap_p: 0.001\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据已完成。Worst 档下此实验是 within-architecture cross-benchmark（仍是 OpenVLA），\n      不解决 RC4 的 cross-architecture concern。Reviewer：\"从 LIBERO-Goal 换到 LIBERO-Spatial\n      只是换了 task suite 不是换了 VLA 架构——这不回答 'does it generalize across architectures'。\"\n      Spatial 的 trained-untrained delta（best-vs-best）=0.023（imgmean）/ 0.040（lastpre）\n      小于 Goal 的 0.015/0.069。退一步看，R² exit collapse 在 D102 更新后被重新定义为\n      VLM→VLA transition effect——但 LIBERO-Spatial 和 Goal 都用同一个 OpenVLA checkpoint（已是 VLA），\n      所以 trained vs untrained（OXE vs LIBERO-finetuned）的 delta 本就该小（VLA→VLA transition）。\n      这与 D102 结论一致但在 worst tier 下被解读为 \"further fine-tuning doesn't change much\n      = fine-tuning doesn't matter much = your study of fine-tuning effects is studying something trivial。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Benchmark Comparison (OpenVLA Only)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Delta (imgmean best-vs-best)\", \"Delta (lastpre best-vs-best)\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LIBERO-Goal\", \"0.015\", \"0.069\", \"Moderate; only architecture tested\"]\n          - [\"LIBERO-Spatial\", \"0.023\", \"0.040\", \"Small; confirms VLA→VLA transition minimal\"]\n          - [\"Implication\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Within-arch replication, not cross-arch validation\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side R² curves for Goal vs Spatial 标注 both are OpenVLA\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cross-benchmark replication 有价值但不解决 cross-architecture gap。D102 framing 下\n      small delta 是 expected（VLA→VLA），但 reviewer 会用此攻击：\"如果进一步 finetuning\n      不 substantially change representations，studying finetuning effects 的意义何在？\"\n\n  - name: \"Full-layer R² scan\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations = 132 probes 的 R² 全层扫描\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 8, R2: 0.655}\n      trained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 13, R2: 0.678}\n      untrained_image_mean_peak: {layer: 0, R2: 0.640}\n      untrained_last_preaction_peak: {layer: 32, R2: 0.609}\n      trained_exit_R2_lastpre: 0.422\n      untrained_exit_R2_lastpre: 0.545\n      exit_collapse_delta_lastpre: 0.256\n      best_vs_best_lastpre_delta: 0.069\n      best_vs_best_lastpre_p: 0.0001\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变（OpenVLA 单架构）。这是 R² exit collapse 的源头实验。D100 NLP control 已排除\n      generic fine-tuning confound（Llama-2-chat ΔR²=0.000），D102 将其定义为 VLM→VLA transition effect。\n      但 worst-tier reviewer 反转 D100/D102：\n      \"D100 证明 NLP finetuning 不产生 exit collapse——好。但这只说明 exit collapse 需要 action training，\n      不说明它有 functional significance。VLM→VLA transition 当然改变 exit layer——action head 需要从\n      exit layer decode 7-DOF actions，这不是 routing 'discovery' 而是 'the model learned to produce actions\n      and the last layer reflects that'。你的 R² probe 测量的是 Ridge regression 从 hidden states 预测 actions\n      的能力——exit layer R² 下降只是说明 action-relevant information 被 'consumed' by action decoding，\n      不是被 'discarded' by routing mechanism。这是 trivially expected under any encoder-decoder framework。\"\n      Worst reviewer 要求 behavioral evidence：如果 exit collapse 是 functional routing，\n      ablating exit-layer representations 应该 disproportionately affect task performance——但这从未被测试。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"R² Exit Collapse with D100/D102 Context (Worst-Tier)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Peak R²\", \"Exit R²\", \"Δ\", \"Worst Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"VLA trained\", \"0.678 (L13)\", \"0.422 (L32)\", \"0.256\", \"Action head 'consumes' info — trivially expected\"]\n          - [\"OXE untrained\", \"0.609 (L32)\", \"0.609 (L32)\", \"0.000\", \"No exit collapse — consistent with VLA→VLA null\"]\n          - [\"Llama-2-chat (D100)\", \"0.156 (all)\", \"0.156 (all)\", \"0.000\", \"NLP: flat noise floor, no action info anywhere\"]\n          - [\"Random init\", \"0.640 (L0)\", \"~0 (L10-L13)\", \"pathological\", \"Not valid control — random weights meaningless\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer R² curves with NLP control flat line at 0.155, annotated 'trivially expected action consumption'\"\n    analysis: |\n      D100 NLP control 排除了 generic fine-tuning confound，这是论文的防御性胜利。但 worst reviewer\n      的 next-level 攻击——exit collapse 是 \"action consumption\" 而非 \"routing mechanism\"——\n      仍然 stands without behavioral validation。Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge 这个区分\n      并 position exit collapse 为 \"diagnostic indicator of action training stage\" 而非 \"mechanistic finding\"。\n\n  - name: \"CLIP-ViT pretraining control\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP 区分 VL pretraining vs encoder quality\"\n    expected_results:\n      clip_rsa: 0.557\n      clip_R2: 0.587\n      dino_cls_rsa: 0.692\n      dino_cls_R2: 0.634\n      projector_R2: 0.630\n      vl_pretraining_not_superior: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据已完成：CLIP < DINO in both RSA and R²。VL pretraining 不优于 self-supervised。\n      Worst 档延伸攻击：\"CLIP < DINO 说明 language-supervised pretraining 不帮助 action representation。\n      那为什么 VLA 要用 language-supervised encoder（SigLIP）而非 self-supervised（DINO）？更关键的是：\n      如果最好的 action-relevant encoder 不需要 language，你们花整篇论文研究 instruction routing\n      的 practical relevance 在哪里？Instructions 在 VLA 中可能是 overhead 而非 feature。\n      你们应该研究为什么 VLA 不用 DINO 作为 encoder，而非研究 instruction 如何 route through LLM。\"\n      这直接挑战论文 premise 而非 findings——worst tier 下论文可能被判 \"interesting but\n      fundamentally misdirected\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Encoder Quality vs Language Supervision\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder\", \"RSA\", \"R²\", \"Has Language?\", \"Worst Implication\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"DINO cls\", \"0.692\", \"0.634\", \"No\", \"Best in both — language supervision unnecessary\"]\n          - [\"SigLIP+Proj\", \"0.615\", \"0.630\", \"Yes\", \"VL pretraining inferior to DINO\"]\n          - [\"CLIP ViT-L\", \"0.557\", \"0.587\", \"Yes\", \"Worst VL encoder\"]\n          - [\"Implication\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \"Language supervision may hurt encoder quality\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"DINO vs VL encoders scatter plot — DINO dominates upper-right corner\"\n    analysis: |\n      CLIP control 结果在 worst tier 下不仅否定 VL pretraining superiority，更挑战整篇论文的\n      motivation。Framework reframe 可以 spin 为 \"framework reveals that language supervision\n      and action quality are decoupled\" 但这是 defensive 而非 proactive contribution。\n\n  - name: \"Branch-split RSA\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"DinoSigLIP fused backbone 中 DINOv2 vs SigLIP branch 分离\"\n    expected_results:\n      dinov2_branch_rsa: 0.619\n      siglip_branch_rsa: 0.621\n      fused_rsa: 0.634\n      post_projector_rsa: 0.615\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据不变。DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP in fused backbone（Δ<0.002）。Worst 档下此实验只适用于\n      OpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP 架构。TracVLA 和 NORA 用完全不同的 vision encoders，\n      branch-split 不可迁移。Reviewer：\"这是 architecture-specific implementation detail，\n      不是 generalizable finding。在 8-page 限制下应移到 appendix。\"\n      在 diagnostic framework reframe 下可保留为 \"framework 能做 sub-encoder analysis\" demo，\n      但 0.5 段就够了。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Architecture-specific detail，appendix material。Framework demo 价值存在但不值得 main text 篇幅。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture R² Exit Collapse Matrix (D096/D099/D102)\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_r2_matrix\"\n    description: \"3 架构 × 4 suite 的 R² exit collapse — D102 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 二元分离\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_cells: 10\n      vlm_to_vla_cells: 6\n      vlm_to_vla_all_substantial: true\n      vlm_to_vla_delta_range: [0.156, 0.455]\n      vla_to_vla_cells: 4\n      vla_to_vla_none_substantial: true\n      vla_to_vla_delta_range: [0.033, 0.086]\n      nlp_control_delta: 0.000\n      binary_separation: \"VLM→VLA 6/6 vs VLA→VLA 0/4\"\n      tracvla_goal_delta: 0.228\n      tracvla_spatial_delta: 0.138\n      tracvla_object_delta: 0.294\n      tracvla_long_delta: 0.198\n      nora_goal_delta: 0.691\n      nora_spatial_delta: 0.302\n      openvla_goal_delta: 0.086\n      openvla_spatial_delta: 0.037\n      openvla_object_delta: 0.037\n      openvla_long_delta: 0.033\n    result_rationale: |\n      D102 更新后数据清晰：VLM→VLA transition 6/6 一致（Δ=0.156-0.455），VLA→VLA 0/4 超过 Δ>0.10\n      阈值（Δ=0.033-0.086）。v3 MCCV 修正了 train-test leakage。D100 NLP control ΔR²=0.000\n      排除了 generic fine-tuning confound。\n      \n      但 worst-tier reviewer 用 D102 的 clean binary 反过来攻击：\n      \"你们自己证明了 exit collapse 是 one-time VLM→VLA transition artifact。这很好，但：\n      (1) 这不是 mechanism discovery——当你把 language model 变成 action model，出口层表征\n      当然会重组。任何 domain adaptation（NLP→vision, text→audio）都可能产生类似 transition effects。\n      你排除了 NLP finetuning，但没排除其他 domain adaptation scenarios（e.g., LLM→code generation）。\n      (2) 作为 diagnostic tool 的价值有限：exit collapse 只告诉你 'this model was once a VLM\n      that got converted to VLA'——但在实践中你已经知道这一点（你知道模型的 training pipeline）。\n      什么时候 practitioner 需要一个 tool 来判断 '我的模型是不是 VLA'？\n      (3) VLA→VLA finetuning 无 exit collapse（0/4）说明它不是 ongoing routing optimization 的\n      indicator——它只是 initial adaptation 的 one-time marker。一个只出现一次的 diagnostic \n      不能用于 iterative VLA development。\n      (4) Magnitude 仍然高度 variable（0.156-0.691, 4.4x range even within VLM→VLA cells），\n      NORA 的 0.691 是 outlier（3x median）。Architecture-independent 的 direction 但\n      architecture-dependent 的 magnitude——这降低了作为 quantitative diagnostic 的 precision。\"\n\n      D100 NLP control 是 good defense 但不足以救 worst tier——因为 reviewer 的攻击不是\n      \"exit collapse is generic fine-tuning\" 而是 \"exit collapse is trivially expected VLM→VLA transition\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"R² Exit Collapse: D102 Binary Separation (Worst-Tier Reinterpretation)\"\n        columns: [\"Transition Type\", \"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Δ (peak-exit)\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"TracVLA (Phi-3→VLA)\", \"Goal\", \"0.228\", \"Expected: domain adaptation reorganization\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"TracVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.138\", \"Expected: same mechanism\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"TracVLA\", \"Object\", \"0.294\", \"Expected: same mechanism\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"TracVLA\", \"Long\", \"0.198\", \"Expected: same mechanism\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"NORA (Qwen2.5→VLA)\", \"Goal\", \"0.691\", \"Outlier: 3x median, architecture-specific\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA\", \"NORA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.302\", \"Expected: consistent with NORA pattern\"]\n          - [\"VLA→VLA\", \"OpenVLA (OXE→LIBERO)\", \"Goal\", \"0.086\", \"Below threshold: no new collapse\"]\n          - [\"VLA→VLA\", \"OpenVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"0.037\", \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"]\n          - [\"VLA→VLA\", \"OpenVLA\", \"Object\", \"0.037\", \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"]\n          - [\"VLA→VLA\", \"OpenVLA\", \"Long\", \"0.033\", \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"]\n      - title: \"Exit Collapse Diagnostic Value Assessment\"\n        columns: [\"Question\", \"Answer\", \"Practical Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Does model show VLM→VLA transition?\", \"Yes, 6/6 cells\", \"Low: practitioner already knows training history\"]\n          - [\"Can it track ongoing optimization?\", \"No, 0/4 VLA→VLA cells\", \"Zero: one-time marker only\"]\n          - [\"Is magnitude calibrated?\", \"No, 4.4x range within VLM→VLA\", \"Low: cannot compare across architectures\"]\n          - [\"Does NLP control exclude confound?\", \"Yes, D100 ΔR²=0.000\", \"Defensive win but doesn't add value\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap split into VLM→VLA (warm) vs VLA→VLA (cold) blocks — clean separation but 'trivially expected' annotation\"\n      - \"NORA Goal outlier at 0.691 circled with '3x median' annotation\"\n    analysis: |\n      D102 binary separation 是 scientifically clean 但 worst-tier reviewer 把 clean result\n      重新定义为 trivial result。NLP control 是 necessary defense 但不 sufficient to elevate\n      contribution。Framework reframe：exit collapse 降为 \"one-time transition marker detected\n      by framework\" 而非 \"architecture-independent routing signature\"。价值在 framework 能\n      systematically detect transition effects 而非 the specific effect detected。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture L1 Attention (D090 Base-Model vs Training)\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_l1_attention\"\n    description: \"3 架构 L1 instruction-dominant heads — D090 证明 base-model-dependent\"\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_trained: 23\n      openvla_oxe_untrained: 26\n      tracvla_trained: [27, 30]\n      tracvla_untrained_vlm: 32\n      nora_trained: [12, 13]\n      nora_untrained_vlm: [13, 14]\n      training_effect_on_l1: \"none or negative\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      D090 发现 L1 head count 是 base-model-dependent。Worst tier 核心攻击：\n      \"L1 routing gradient（0→9→24 heads）是论文最 visually striking 的结果，但你们自己证明了\n      它不是训练学到的。TracVLA untrained（纯 VLM）已 32/32，训练反而减少到 27-30（repurposing）。\n      NORA untrained 已 13-14/16，训练无变化。OpenVLA 的 0→24 gradient 只是 random init vs\n      pretrained 的差异——任何 pretrained LLM 都有 instruction attention heads，不需要 VLA training。\n      \n      这意味着论文最核心的 visual result（Figure X 的 attention head gradient）不能 claim\n      是 VLA training 的贡献。读者看到这个图会以为训练创造了 routing——但实际上 routing 来自\n      language pretraining。这是 misleading framing，即使你在正文中有 caveat。\"\n      \n      D090 后 remaining training-induced effects 只剩 exit collapse 和 CF sensitivity。\n      Reviewer 总结：\"After D090, VLA training's unique contribution is one transition artifact\n      (exit collapse) and one baseline-confounded sensitivity measure (CF). This is too thin\n      for a full paper at a top robotics venue.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"L1 Heads: Training Contributes Nothing (D090 Worst Reading)\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Base Model\", \"Trained\", \"Untrained\", \"Training Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Llama-2-7B\", \"24/32\", \"0/32 (random init)\", \"Artifact: random has no LM\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"OXE-pretrained\", \"24/32\", \"25/32 (OXE)\", \"-1: OXE already saturated\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Phi-3-mini\", \"27-30/32\", \"32/32 (VLM base)\", \"-2 to -5: training REDUCES\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Qwen2.5-VL-3B\", \"12-13/16\", \"13-14/16\", \"-1: no training effect\"]\n      - title: \"Contribution Audit After D090\"\n        columns: [\"Originally Claimed\", \"Post-D090 Status\", \"Remaining Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"L1 routing gradient (0→9→24)\", \"REMOVED: base-model artifact\", \"Zero\"]\n          - [\"Bookend attention pattern\", \"WEAKENED: entry from base model\", \"Exit engagement only\"]\n          - [\"R² exit collapse\", \"Retained: training-induced\", \"Thin — one-time transition\"]\n          - [\"CF sensitivity\", \"Retained: training-induced\", \"Thin — unfair baselines\"]\n          - [\"Experimental framework\", \"Intact\", \"Main surviving contribution\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Before/After D090 contribution diagram — L1 routing crossed out, remaining pillars marked 'questionable'\"\n    analysis: |\n      D090 是论文最大的 self-inflicted wound。Framework reframe 试图把 D090 从 weakness 转为\n      \"framework's key capability: distinguishing training-induced from pre-existing\"——\n      但 reviewer 可能看穿这个 rhetorical move。核心问题：能区分 training vs pretraining\n      effects 是 methodology 贡献，但 CoRL 评审 findings 而非 methods。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Architecture Counterfactual Sensitivity\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_arch_cf\"\n    description: \"3 架构 CF sensitivity — trained vs untrained 对比\"\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_goal_trained_d: 1.182\n      openvla_goal_untrained_d: 1.048\n      openvla_spatial_trained_d: 1.173\n      openvla_spatial_untrained_d: 0.936\n      tracvla_goal_trained_d: 1.524\n      tracvla_goal_untrained_cos: 0.153\n      nora_goal_trained_cos: 1.0\n      nora_goal_untrained_cos: 0.081\n      incommensurable_pairs: 5\n      fair_comparison_pairs: 2\n      openvla_goal_fair_delta: 0.134\n      openvla_spatial_fair_delta: 0.237\n    result_rationale: |\n      D097/D099 修正后，CF sensitivity 的 cross-architecture 对比面临 incommensurability 问题：\n      TracVLA/NORA untrained 无法生成 actions（cosine in hidden space），trained 用 Cohen's d\n      in action space——两个 metrics 不可直接比较。只有 OpenVLA 的 trained + untrained 都能生成\n      actions，可用同一 metric 比较。\n\n      Worst-tier reviewer 攻击：\n      \"CF sensitivity 是你们仅存的两个 training-induced effects 之一（D090 后），但：\n      (1) 你们自己承认 5/7 cross-architecture comparisons 使用 incommensurable metrics（Cohen's d\n      vs cosine distance）。你不能 claim 'training amplifies CF sensitivity' 如果 trained 和\n      untrained 用不同 metrics 测量——这不是 methodological nuance，这是 fundamental flaw。\n      (2) 唯一公平对比（OpenVLA Goal/Spatial）显示 Δ=+0.13/+0.24，即 trained 比 untrained\n      高 12%/25%。但 OpenVLA untrained 是 OXE-pretrained VLA（已有 strong CF d=1.048），\n      所以 'training amplification' 是 VLA→VLA marginal improvement 而非 VLM→VLA dramatic change。\n      (3) 'Empty instruction produces largest deviation' 在 6/8 settings——这不需要 VLA-specific\n      routing 来解释。任何 conditioned generative model 在 input 被完全移除时 output 会 change most。\n      这是 conditioning 的 definition 而非 routing mechanism。\n      (4) CF sensitivity 没有 behavioral grounding：output changes（d=0.65-1.5）是否\n      导致 task failure？如果 perturbed instructions 产生 different but equally valid actions，\n      CF sensitivity 不是 routing evidence 而是 representational noise。\n      缺少 behavioral validation（closed-loop success rate under perturbation）是 near-fatal\n      for CoRL submission。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"CF Sensitivity: Incommensurability Problem\"\n        columns: [\"Architecture\", \"Suite\", \"Trained Metric\", \"Untrained Metric\", \"Comparable?\", \"Fair Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Goal\", \"d=1.182\", \"d=1.048\", \"Yes\", \"+0.134 (12%)\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"d=1.173\", \"d=0.936\", \"Yes\", \"+0.237 (25%)\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Goal\", \"d=1.524\", \"cos=0.153\", \"No\", \"Incommensurable\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Spatial\", \"d=1.333\", \"cos=0.180\", \"No\", \"Incommensurable\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Object\", \"d=1.212\", \"cos=0.185\", \"No\", \"Incommensurable\"]\n          - [\"TracVLA\", \"Long\", \"d=1.473\", \"cos=0.173\", \"No\", \"Incommensurable\"]\n          - [\"NORA\", \"Goal\", \"cos=1.0 (sat.)\", \"cos=0.081\", \"Partially\", \"Saturated — ceiling artifact?\"]\n      - title: \"CF Sensitivity: Missing Behavioral Validation\"\n        columns: [\"What CF Shows\", \"What Reviewer Wants\", \"Gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Output direction changes (d>0.5)\", \"Task success rate drops\", \"No closed-loop data\"]\n          - [\"Empty > wrong > shuffled > para\", \"Perturbation severity → failure rate correlation\", \"No behavioral grounding\"]\n          - [\"ΔMSE≈0 vs ground-truth\", \"Action quality under perturbation\", \"MSE≈0 suggests no quality impact\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bars with 5/7 pairs marked 'INCOMMENSURABLE' in red\"\n      - \"ΔMSE≈0 annotated as 'CF changes direction but not quality — no functional consequence'\"\n    analysis: |\n      CF sensitivity 在 worst tier 下被 double-attacked: incommensurable metrics + no behavioral\n      grounding。ΔMSE≈0 (ground-truth error unchanged under ablation) is particularly damaging——\n      it suggests CF perturbation changes output direction without degrading quality，\n      supporting \"information-computation dissociation\" (Hewitt & Liang 2019) interpretation\n      that routing modulates output but doesn't encode task-critical information。\n      Framework reframe：CF analysis 降为 \"framework's perturbation analysis capability\"，\n      behavioral validation 列为 \"critical future work\"。\n\n  - name: \"Three-Tier Routing Gradient (D094)\"\n    plan_id: \"three_tier_gradient\"\n    description: \"VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA → task-finetuned VLA 三层级路由梯度\"\n    expected_results:\n      tier1_models: [\"Phi-3-Vision\", \"Qwen2.5-VL\", \"random init Llama-2\"]\n      tier1_l1_heads: [32, 14, 0]\n      tier1_cf_max_cos: 0.19\n      tier1_exit_collapse: false\n      tier2_model: \"openvla-7b (OXE)\"\n      tier2_l1_heads: 25\n      tier2_cf_d: 1.048\n      tier2_exit_collapse: false\n      tier3_l1_heads: [24, 30, 13]\n      tier3_exit_collapse_vlm_origin: true\n      tier3_exit_collapse_vla_origin: false\n      tier2_n_datapoints: 1\n    result_rationale: |\n      三层级梯度被 worst reviewer 驳为 post-hoc narrative with N=1 at Tier-2。\n      \n      攻击 1 — 统计力不足：\"Tier-2 只有一个数据点（openvla-7b OXE pretrained）。要建立 gradient\n      你需要 at minimum 3 个独立的 OXE-pretrained 或 general-pretrained VLA checkpoints 来\n      验证 Tier-2 不是 openvla-7b specific。Three points don't make a gradient if the middle\n      one is N=1——那是 step function with one interpolation point。\"\n      \n      攻击 2 — L1 heads 在 tiers 间不单调：\"Tier-1 Phi-3-Vision = 32/32, Tier-2 OXE = 25/32,\n      Tier-3 TracVLA = 27-30/32。Tier-1 > Tier-2 ≈ Tier-3——这不是 gradient，这是 'base model\n      already saturated then training reduces some heads'。L1 head count 不支持 gradient narrative。\"\n      \n      攻击 3 — Exit collapse 不支持 gradient：\"Tier-2 无 exit collapse, Tier-3 有 exit collapse\n      只在 VLM→VLA origin models——这是 binary transition 不是 gradient。如果 Tier-3 只在\n      VLM-origin 有 collapse 而 VLA-origin 没有，那 'gradient' 应该有 collapse 强度在 Tier-2→Tier-3\n      increasing——但 Tier-2 = 0, Tier-3 (VLA origin) = 0。只有 Tier-3 (VLM origin) 有 collapse。\n      这是 binary (VLM→VLA collapse exists / doesn't) 不是 three-tier gradient。\"\n      \n      攻击 4 — libero_finetuned attention data 反驳 gradient：\"L31 exit engagement 从 bridge-VLA\n      (18 heads) 到 libero-finetuned (0 heads)——further specialization REDUCES exit routing。\n      Gradient predicts 'more training = more routing' 但 data shows opposite at exit layer。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Three-Tier Gradient: N=1 at Tier-2\"\n        columns: [\"Tier\", \"N Models\", \"Key Metrics\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Tier 1 (VLM)\", \"3+\", \"L1: 0-32; CF<0.2; no collapse\", \"Adequate N but heterogeneous (0 vs 32 heads)\"]\n          - [\"Tier 2 (General VLA)\", \"1 ONLY\", \"L1: 25; CF d=1.05; no collapse\", \"N=1 — cannot establish gradient\"]\n          - [\"Tier 3 (Task VLA)\", \"~10 cells\", \"L1: 13-30; CF d>0.45; collapse if VLM-origin\", \"Adequate N but split by origin\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Gradient diagram with Tier-2 marked 'N=1' and dashed connections\"\n      - \"L1 head count across tiers showing non-monotonic pattern (Phi-3: 32→25→30)\"\n    analysis: |\n      Three-tier gradient 必须移除或降为 \"preliminary observation with N=1 at intermediate tier\"。\n      Framework reframe：不 claim gradient，改为 \"framework enables stage-wise comparison\"——\n      contribute methodology for comparing training stages, not the gradient finding itself.\n\n  - name: \"NLP Finetuning Control (D100)\"\n    plan_id: \"nlp_finetuning_control\"\n    description: \"Llama-2-7b-chat R² profile 排除 generic fine-tuning confound\"\n    expected_results:\n      peak_r2: 0.1555\n      exit_r2: 0.1555\n      delta_r2: 0.000\n      profile_shape: \"flat constant across all 32 layers\"\n      r2_range: [0.1547, 0.1555]\n      phi3_nlp_delta: 0.000\n      qwen_nlp_delta: 0.000\n    result_rationale: |\n      D100 结果 clean：三个 NLP-finetuned LLM（Llama-2-chat, Phi-3-instruct, Qwen2.5-instruct）\n      均 ΔR²=0.000，flat R²≈0.155 noise floor。这排除了 \"exit collapse is generic fine-tuning artifact\"。\n\n      但 worst-tier reviewer 不被 impressed：\n      \"D100 是 good negative control，我们接受 exit collapse 不是 generic fine-tuning。\n      但这不能 elevate exit collapse 为 interesting finding——它只从 'might be generic artifact'\n      升级为 'VLA-specific but trivially expected'。当你训练一个 language model 来 predict\n      7-DOF robot actions，exit layer 表征当然会被 action training reshape。\n      R²≈0.155 in NLP models 只是说明 NLP models 没有 action-relevant information 在任何层\n      （Ridge 只拟合 between-task variance）——当然不会有 exit collapse。\n      你排除了一个 straw-man confound 但没有建立 positive value。\n      A good control experiment answers 'is this finding real?' — yours answers 'is this finding\n      even more trivially explainable than I thought?'  答案是 No，但 the finding is still trivial。\"\n\n      R²=0.155 本身是 between-task variance baseline（10 tasks → Ridge 可拟合 task identity → \n      0.155 R² from 10-way between-task variance alone）——这是 expected 而非 surprising。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"NLP Finetuning Control Results\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Backbone\", \"ΔR²\", \"Profile\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Llama-2-7b-chat\", \"Llama-2-7B\", \"0.000\", \"Flat 0.155\", \"Expected: no action info anywhere\"]\n          - [\"Phi-3-mini-instruct\", \"Phi-3-mini\", \"0.000\", \"Flat 0.155\", \"Expected: same noise floor\"]\n          - [\"Qwen2.5-3B-instruct\", \"Qwen2.5-3B\", \"0.000\", \"Flat 0.155\", \"Expected: same noise floor\"]\n          - [\"VLM→VLA (TracVLA)\", \"Phi-3-mini\", \"0.156-0.294\", \"Exit collapse\", \"VLA-specific but trivially expected\"]\n          - [\"VLA→VLA (OpenVLA)\", \"Llama-2-7B\", \"0.033-0.086\", \"Mild decline\", \"No new collapse in VLA→VLA\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-layer R² with NLP controls as flat lines at 0.155 — 'straw-man excluded' annotation\"\n    analysis: |\n      D100 是 necessary but not sufficient defense。Worst reviewer accepts the control\n      but doesn't give credit for it — \"excluding an obvious confound is minimum bar,\n      not contribution.\" Framework reframe 可以 cite D100 作为 \"framework enables\n      cross-domain comparison\" demo，但 reviewer 的 next-level attack（trivially expected）\n      仍 stands。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-Instruction Classification (C1 Framework)\"\n    plan_id: \"cross_instruction_classification\"\n    description: \"10-way instruction classification 跨层 × 跨条件 — C1 框架核心实验\"\n    expected_results:\n      trained_L1_acc: 0.996\n      trained_L2_to_L31: 1.000\n      llama2base_L1_acc: 0.802\n      llama2base_L5_plus: 1.000\n      untrained_L1_acc: 1.000\n      untrained_L31_acc: 0.820\n      image_mean_all_layers: 0.10\n      loocv_trained: \"100.00±0.00\"\n      loocv_untrained: \"84.76±11.59\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据完整。Worst 档下 C1 被彻底降级：\n      \"10-way classification on 4096-dim features 是 trivially easy。Untrained (random init)\n      L1 也达到 100%——random projection 就能分离 10 个 class。你的 LOOCV 只在 untrained deep layers\n      下降到 85%——这不是 'training improves routing' 而是 'random weights corrupt signal in deep layers'。\n      \n      Image mean = 10% at all layers 是 causal mask guarantee 不是 finding。你自己承认了。\n      \n      三条件对比（trained flat 100%, llama2base saturates L5, untrained decays to 82%）的\n      interpretation 也被质疑：'trained L1=99.6% vs llama2base L1=80.2%' 看起来像 'training\n      creates immediate routing'，但 D090 证明 L1 heads 来自 base model 而非 training。\n      那 99.6% vs 80.2% 的差异可能只反映 VLA fine-tuning 后 feature quality 提升（action-relevant\n      features are more linearly separable）而非 routing reorganization。\n      \n      贡献在 methodology（factorial design + 4 methods）而非 findings。但 methodology 贡献在\n      CoRL 通常只值 weak accept——CoRL 偏好 systems + behavioral results。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Instruction Classification: Trivially Easy?\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"L1 Acc\", \"L31 Acc\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Trained\", \"99.6%\", \"100%\", \"Flat 100% = ceiling effect, no gradient to analyze\"]\n          - [\"Llama-2 base\", \"80.2%\", \"100%\", \"LM pretraining provides separability, not VLA training\"]\n          - [\"Untrained (random)\", \"100%\", \"82%\", \"Even random features separate 10 classes at L1\"]\n          - [\"Image mean\", \"10%\", \"10%\", \"Causal mask guarantee, not finding\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-condition probe curves annotated with 'trivially easy' at ceiling regions\"\n    analysis: |\n      C1 的 experimental framework 是 reframe 后的 primary contribution。但 cross-instruction\n      classification 作为 framework demo 的问题：10-way on 4096d 太 easy，不 demonstrate\n      framework 在 harder settings 下的 value。需要更 challenging classification tasks\n      或 fine-grained metrics 来 justify framework utility。\n\n  - name: \"Head Ablation and Specificity Controls\"\n    plan_id: \"head_ablation_suite\"\n    description: \"L1 attention head ablation 实验套件 — 验证 instruction-dominant heads 的功能特异性\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_r2_L13: 0.676\n      ablate_24_instr_r2_L13: 0.676\n      ablate_24_random_r2_L13: 0.664\n      random_24_z_score: -2.73\n      specificity_ratio: 1.08\n      instruction_d: 0.651\n      random_24_d: 0.601\n      image_24_d: 0.580\n      gt_error_delta_mse: -0.001\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据已完成。Worst 档下 ablation 结果被严厉解读：\n      \n      (1) Specificity ratio = 1.08x 极弱：\"instruction-dominant 24 heads 的 per-head effect\n      不比 random 24 heads 大多少（z=-2.73 但 effect size tiny）。任何 24/32 heads ablation\n      产生 similar or larger R² increase（random 24 mean delta = 0.077 > instruction 24 delta = 0.042）。\n      Instruction-dominant heads 不是 special——they're 75% of all heads，removing ANY 75%\n      of heads produces similar effects。\"\n      \n      (2) ΔMSE≈0 vs ground-truth 是 worst tier 最致命的 finding：\"你 ablate 24 instruction-dominant\n      heads，action outputs change direction (d=0.65) 但 ground-truth error 不变（ΔMSE=-0.001, p=0.52）。\n      这意味着 instruction routing 对 action quality 无影响——perturbation 改变 output 方向\n      但不改变 output 质量。这直接证明 CF sensitivity 缺乏 functional significance。\n      如果移除 75% 的 'instruction routing heads' 对 action quality 无影响，\n      那 instruction routing 在 action generation 中可能是 redundant mechanism。\"\n      \n      (3) Information-computation dissociation 解读在 worst tier 下被反转：论文 cite Hewitt & Liang 2019\n      作为 \"ΔMSE≈0 is expected under dissociation\"，但 reviewer 说：\n      \"Hewitt & Liang 的 point 是 probe results don't prove representation is functionally used。\n      你在用他们的 framework 来 excuse 你的 negative result。ΔMSE≈0 doesn't support 'routing\n      modulates without degrading'——it supports 'routing doesn't matter for output quality'。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Head Ablation: No Functional Specificity\"\n        columns: [\"Ablation Group\", \"24h d\", \"Per-head d\", \"GT ΔMSE\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Instr-dominant 24\", \"0.651\", \"0.027\", \"-0.001 (p=0.52)\", \"Changes direction, not quality\"]\n          - [\"Random 24 (avg)\", \"0.601\", \"0.025\", \"similar\", \"Any 24 heads produce similar effect\"]\n          - [\"Image-dominant 24\", \"0.580\", \"0.024\", \"similar\", \"No group specificity\"]\n          - [\"Control 8 (random)\", \"0.410\", \"0.051\", \"similar\", \"Per-head effect LARGER in control\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ΔMSE≈0 highlighted as 'no functional consequence of instruction routing ablation'\"\n    analysis: |\n      Head ablation suite is worst tier's most damaging evidence against CF sensitivity as\n      functional routing. ΔMSE≈0 + specificity ratio 1.08x together argue that instruction\n      routing (as measured by attention head dominance) has no disproportionate functional role.\n      Framework reframe 很难 rescue this——the framework's own ablation tool reveals that\n      the effect it detected (instruction routing) is not functionally specific.\n\n  - name: \"Counterfactual Token Overlap and Trajectory-Level Analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"cf_detailed_analysis\"\n    description: \"CF perturbation 的 token overlap, trajectory-level d, 和 ΔMSE 扩展分析\"\n    expected_results:\n      token_overlap_spearman: 1.0\n      empty_d_token: 0.968\n      empty_d_trajectory: 3.438\n      wrong_d_token: 0.844\n      wrong_d_trajectory: 3.798\n      shuffled_d_token: 0.625\n      shuffled_d_trajectory: 2.595\n      para_d_token: 0.697\n      para_d_trajectory: 2.131\n      inflation_factor_mean: 0.245\n      gt_mse_original: 0.498\n      gt_mse_top24_ablated: 0.497\n      gt_mse_delta: -0.001\n    result_rationale: |\n      数据已完成。Worst 档下 token overlap analysis 被反过来用：\n      \n      \"Spearman ρ=1.0 between token novelty and Cohen's d 说明 CF sensitivity 完全由\n      lexical/positional distance 驱动，不是 semantic distance。Empty（最大 token novelty）→\n      largest d，shuffled（same tokens, different order）→ moderate d，paraphrased（high overlap）→\n      smallest d。这不是 'the model understands instruction semantics'——这是 'the model responds\n      to surface-level token changes'。任何 autoregressive language model 都会如此。\"\n      \n      Trajectory-level d（2.1-3.8）远大于 token-level d（0.6-0.97）——inflation factor ~4x。\n      Worst reviewer：\"trajectory-level inflation 说明 per-timestep effects 累积——这不是\n      'stronger evidence of routing' 而是 'autocorrelation amplification'。每个 timestep\n      的小 perturbation 通过 temporal autocorrelation 累积成大 trajectory difference，\n      这是 dynamical systems 的 trivial property 不是 routing evidence。\"\n      \n      GT MSE unchanged（0.498 vs 0.497）再次确认 CF perturbation 不影响 action quality。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Token Overlap → Cohen's d: Surface-Level Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"Perturbation\", \"Token Novelty\", \"Token d\", \"Traj d\", \"Worst Reading\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"empty\", \"1.0\", \"0.968\", \"3.438\", \"Max novelty → max effect: lexical, not semantic\"]\n          - [\"wrong\", \"0.83\", \"0.844\", \"3.798\", \"High novelty → high effect\"]\n          - [\"paraphrased\", \"0.47\", \"0.697\", \"2.131\", \"Low novelty → low effect\"]\n          - [\"shuffled\", \"0.0\", \"0.625\", \"2.595\", \"Zero novelty but positional change → moderate\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Token novelty vs d scatter with ρ=1.0 line — annotated 'surface-level sensitivity, not semantic routing'\"\n    analysis: |\n      ρ=1.0 token-novelty/d correlation is worst-tier's strongest argument that CF sensitivity\n      measures lexical sensitivity rather than semantic routing. Framework reframe has no good\n      counter — the framework's own analysis reveals CF is surface-level. Could argue \"shuffled\n      same tokens different order still produces d=0.63\" as evidence of positional sensitivity\n      beyond pure lexical, but this is weak defense.\n\n  - name: \"D090 Synthesis: What VLA Training Actually Contributes\"\n    plan_id: \"d090_contribution_synthesis\"\n    description: \"综合评估：D090 后论文的 residual contribution\"\n    expected_results:\n      training_induced_effects: [\"R² exit collapse (VLM→VLA only)\", \"CF sensitivity (unfair baselines)\"]\n      base_model_effects: [\"L1 head count\", \"deep-layer probe stability\"]\n      removed_contributions: [\"L1 routing gradient\", \"attention bookend pattern (entry component)\"]\n      remaining_unique: \"1-2 effects, both with caveats\"\n      reviewer_avg_score: [4.0, 5.5]\n      strong_reject_count: [1, 2]\n      accept_probability: [0.05, 0.20]\n      claims_surviving: [0.5, 1.5]\n    result_rationale: |\n      D090 后 contribution audit 在 worst tier 下：\n      \n      Training-induced（retained but weakened）:\n      - R² exit collapse：6/6 VLM→VLA, 0/4 VLA→VLA — clean binary。D100 排除 NLP confound。\n        但 worst reviewer 视为 \"trivially expected transition artifact\"。\n      - CF sensitivity：d≥0.45 in all trained settings。但 incommensurable baselines（5/7 pairs），\n        ρ=1.0 token-novelty correlation（surface-level），ΔMSE≈0（no functional consequence）。\n      \n      Base-model-dependent（removed from contribution）:\n      - L1 head count：Phi-3 32/32 untrained, NORA 13/16 untrained — not training-induced。\n      - Deep-layer stability：Llama-2 base also stable（100% L5+）— from LM pretraining。\n      \n      Reviewer score prediction:\n      - R1（expects behavioral results）：4/10 — \"descriptive analysis without actionable insight,\n        CoRL expects at minimum open-loop policy evaluation.\"\n      - R2（appreciates methodology）：6/10 — \"framework is solid and systematic, cross-architecture\n        validation is thorough engineering. But findings are thin after D090 self-critique.\"\n      - R3（generalizability focus）：4/10 — \"exit collapse magnitude 4.4x range within VLM→VLA,\n        CF baselines incommensurable. Claims are over-qualified to the point of being unfalsifiable.\"\n      Mean: 4.67. Strong reject: 0-1. Accept probability: 0.10-0.20.\n      \n      Reframe 能做的最大提升：如果 C1 framework 成功 pitch 为 primary contribution（\"first\n      systematic VLA profiling toolkit\"），R2 可能升到 7，但 R1/R3 不变——\n      结果 mean 5.0，borderline reject。需要 AC 同情才有机会。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Worst-Tier Score Prediction\"\n        columns: [\"Reviewer\", \"Score\", \"Primary Concern\", \"Verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"R1 (behavioral)\", \"4\", \"No closed-loop validation; CoRL is robotics venue\", \"Reject\"]\n          - [\"R2 (methodology)\", \"6\", \"Framework solid; findings thin but honest\", \"Weak Accept\"]\n          - [\"R3 (generalizability)\", \"4\", \"Magnitude variance; incommensurable baselines; over-qualified claims\", \"Reject\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"4.67\", \"2 reject + 1 weak accept\", \"Likely Reject\"]\n      - title: \"Reframe Impact on Scores\"\n        columns: [\"Reframe Element\", \"Score Impact\", \"Which Reviewer\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"C1 framework as primary contribution\", \"+1 for R2 only\", \"R2: 6→7\"]\n          - [\"D090 as framework capability demo\", \"+0.5 for R2\", \"R2 already sympathetic\"]\n          - [\"Exit collapse as diagnostic\", \"0 for R1/R3\", \"Doesn't address behavioral gap\"]\n          - [\"Roadmap for closed-loop future work\", \"+0.5 for R1 maybe\", \"R1 may soften to 4.5\"]\n          - [\"Net after reframe\", \"Mean ~5.0\", \"Still borderline reject\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Contribution pyramid after D090: framework base (solid), exit collapse (thin), CF (thin), L1 routing (crossed out)\"\n    analysis: |\n      Worst tier 核心判定：论文 honest analysis (D090) + thorough controls (D100) 是 scientifically\n      commendable 但 strategically devastating。每个 defense 实验排除了一个 confound 但同时削弱了\n      contribution scope。D090 证明 L1 routing 不是训练效果；D100 证明 exit collapse 不是 generic\n      finetuning 但仍被视为 trivial；ΔMSE≈0 证明 ablation 不影响 quality 但被解读为 \"routing\n      doesn't functionally matter\"。\n      \n      Reframe 路径：diagnostic framework + honest empirical characterization。Accept probability\n      0.05-0.20 range。需要 AC 认可 methodology contribution 的 standalone value 才有机会。\n      关键 rebuttal material：(1) representation engineering literature 论证 representational\n      analysis 的独立价值，(2) exit collapse as VLM→VLA binary diagnostic 的 concrete use case\n      （判断 pretraining checkpoint 是否完成 VLA transition），(3) framework reusability 的\n      具体 demonstration（how others can apply it to new VLAs）。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4327d556-6a05-42fb-ae30-82d4a0777322","total_cost_usd":1.22803835,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79362,"cache_read_input_tokens":144610,"output_tokens":21081,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79362,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":20742,"cache_read_input_tokens":67106,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24097},"type":"message"}],"speed"